-02cb0d050764","name":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have a craving for something like the creamy pasta from that Italian place downtown. Find me a copycat recipe."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can help you find a copycat recipe for creamy pasta! To make sure I find the best match, could you tell me the name of the Italian place downtown, or any specific details about the creamy pasta you enjoyed there?"},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"we0eT4mEGQFW0XPZ","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"copycat creamy pasta recipe Italian place downtown"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"A popular copycat creamy pasta recipe inspired by Italian places downtown often involves cooking a blend of Italian sausage, crushed tomatoes, heavy cream, and Parmesan cheese with pasta, as in an easy creamy spaghetti dish. One such recipe includes cooking ground mild Italian sausage, then adding crushed tomatoes, chicken stock, heavy cream, and red pepper flakes, simmering, and cooking uncooked spaghetti directly in the sauce until al dente. Parmesan cheese is then stirred in to make the sauce richly creamy and flavorful, garnished with fresh herbs like parsley or basil before serving.\\n\\nHere is a concise version of this copycat creamy pasta recipe:\\n\\n**Ingredients:**\\n- 1 lb mild Italian sausage (ground)\\n- 12 oz spaghetti (uncooked)\\n- 28 oz crushed tomatoes (canned)\\n- 4 cups chicken stock (32 oz)\\n- 1 cup heavy cream\\n- 1 tsp red pepper flakes\\n- 1 cup grated Parmesan cheese\\n- Salt and pepper to taste\\n- Fresh parsley or basil (garnish)\\n\\n**Instructions:**\\n1. Brown the Italian sausage in a large pot, breaking it up as it cooks.\\n2. Add crushed tomatoes, chicken stock, and heavy cream to the pot; stir to combine.\\n3. Add red pepper flakes, salt, and pepper; bring to a simmer.\\n4. Add uncooked spaghetti, stirring frequently to prevent sticking; cook until al dente and most liquid is absorbed (~10-12 minutes).\\n5. Stir in grated Parmesan until the sauce is creamy.\\n6. Remove from heat, let it thicken a few minutes, then garnish with fresh herbs and serve.\\n\\nThis recipe captures the creamy, rich texture and hearty flavor typical of creamy pasta dishes served at many Italian restaurants in downtown areas. Additional vegetables or spices can be added for customization. If you want a creamy tomato-based pasta without sausage, a similar creamy rosa sauce with ingredients like mushrooms, spinach, fresh tomatoes, and cream is also available as a copycat for Italian places.\\n\\nIf you are looking for a specific restaurant''s copycat creamy pasta downtown, providing the restaurant name or more details might help further tailor the recipe. Otherwise, the above recipe is a widely appreciated template for creamy Italian-style pasta dishes.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"we0eT4mEGQFW0XPZ"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a popular copycat recipe for creamy pasta that''s often found in Italian restaurants! It features Italian sausage, crushed tomatoes, heavy cream, and Parmesan cheese, all cooked with spaghetti. \n\nHere''s a quick overview:\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- 1 lb mild Italian sausage\n- 12 oz spaghetti\n- 28 oz crushed tomatoes\n- 4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 cup heavy cream\n- 1 tsp red pepper flakes\n- 1 cup grated Parmesan cheese\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n- Fresh parsley or basil (garnish)\n\n**Instructions:**\n1. Brown Italian sausage.\n2. Add crushed tomatoes, chicken stock, heavy cream, red pepper flakes, salt, and pepper; simmer.\n3. Add uncooked spaghetti and cook until al dente.\n4. Stir in Parmesan cheese until creamy.\n5. Garnish with fresh herbs and serve.\n\nDoes this sound like what you were craving? If you''d like, I can save this recipe for you or provide the full detailed instructions!"}]}]',1763115407470,1763115407470,'*   **User''s core intent**: To find a copycat recipe for a creamy pasta dish similar to one from an Italian restaurant.\u000a*   **Key actions made**: The AI asked for clarification, then provided a copycat recipe for creamy pasta, including ingredients and a 5-step overview.\u000a*   **Current state**: The AI has presented a recipe and is asking the user for confirmation on its suitability, offering to save it or provide full detailed instructions.');
