scription":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I suddenly remembered, I have cavities and can''t eat desserts. Could you please remove Healthy Hot Chocolate Date Bites from the recipe?"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understand. I will remove the \"Healthy Hot Chocolate Date Bites\" recipe for you. Just a moment."},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"bvYkYXF8HpdvB8co","name":"recipe_searchRecipes","arguments":{"query":"Healthy Hot Chocolate Date Bites"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"recipe_searchRecipes","content":"[{\"id\":\"81a13ce9-d559-4a43-b6b9-3599a8be762e\",\"name\":\"Healthy Hot Chocolate Date Bites\",\"cooking_time\":null,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. If your dates are hard, soak them in warm water for 5–10 minutes, then drain and pat dry.;2. In a food processor, combine the cashews, pitted dates, cocoa powder, chili powder (if using), cinnamon, cayenne (if using), and vanilla extract.;3. Pulse until the mixture comes together and forms a sticky dough. If it’s too dry, add a teaspoon of water. If too wet, add a few more cashews.;4. Pinch off small pieces of dough and roll them into bite-sized balls with your hands.;5. Roll the balls in extra cocoa powder or shredded coconut for a finishing touch.;6. Place the bites on a plate or tray and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes to firm up.;7. Enjoy chilled. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 week, or freeze for longer storage.\",\"ingredients\":\"unsalted cashews: cup 1 , is_optional: ;-18 pitted Medjool dates:  15 , is_optional: ;unsweetened cocoa powder: tablespoons 2 , is_optional: ;mild chili powder: teaspoon 1/4 , is_optional: ;ground cinnamon: teaspoon 1 , is_optional: ;tiny pinch cayenne pepper:   , is_optional: ;pure vanilla extract: teaspoon 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-6a7f4ff5-e3dc-4ae7-a833-686bd7bc2939\",\"name\":\"Mexican Hot Chocolate\",\"cooking_time\":5,\"servings\":9,\"instructions\":\"1. In a storage container, combine the nonfat dry milk powder, cocoa powder, powdered sugar substitute, and ground cinnamon.;2. Mix all ingredients well.;3. Cover the container and store the cocoa mix in a cool, dry place for up to 8 weeks.;4. For each serving, place 1/3 cup of the prepared cocoa mix in a mug.;5. Add 2/3 cup of boiling water to the mug and stir to mix until dissolved.\",\"ingredients\":\"Nonfat dry milk powder: cup 2.75 , is_optional: ;Unsweetened cocoa powder: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Powdered sugar substitute: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Ground cinnamon: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Boiling water: cup 6 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-95ecda10-8425-41dc-81b3-6dbb67754a5f\",\"name\":\"Choco Date Cake\",\"cooking_time\":25,\"servings\":16,\"instructions\":\"1. Combine the dates and water in a saucepan, and bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer, covered, for 10 minutes.;2. Remove from the heat and cool completely.;3. Sift the flour, baking soda and salt together, blending well, then set aside.;4. Cream the butter and sugar together in a medium mixing bowl, until light and fluffy, using an electric mixer set on medium speed.;5. Add the eggs, one at a time, beating well after each addition.;6. Beat in the vanilla.;7. Stir the flour mixture into the creamed mixture, blending well.;8. Stir in the date mixture, oats, and chocolate chips, mixing until well blended.;9. Pour the batter into a greased 13 X 9 X 2-inch baking pan.;10. Bake in a preheated 350 Degree F oven for 35 minutes or until a cake tester or wooden pick inserted in the center of the cake comes out clean.;11. Cool in the pan on a wire rack.;12. Serve the cake topped with sweetened whipped cream.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pitted Dates: oz 8 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 1.25 , is_optional: ;Unbleached All-Purpose Flour: cup 1.25 , is_optional: ;Baking Soda: tsp 1.25 , is_optional: ;Salt: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Butter: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;Sugar: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Eggs:  2 , is_optional: ;Vanilla: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Quick Cooking Oats: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Semi-Sweet Chocolate Chips: oz 6 , is_optional: ;Sweetened Whipped Cream:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3451cac9-522b-461d-8e41-fe293e5e58a0\",\"name\":\"Date & Nut Bites\",\"cooking_time\":15,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Combine all ingredients in a processor.;2. Process until finely chopped.;3. Pat into a serving container.;4. Cover until needed.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pitted dates: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Dried apricots: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Walnuts: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;Almonds: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;Cinnamon: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Ginger: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Orange juice: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;Red kosher wine: tbsp 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-80fa5d72-b940-4292-b8a9-992252671d2c\",\"name\":\"Chocolate Date Truffles\",\"cooking_time\":30,\"servings\":30,\"instructions\":\"1. In a medium saucepan over very low heat, melt chocolate chips, stirring constantly. Remove from heat.;2. Stir in vanilla wafers, 1/2 cup powdered sugar, yogurt, and almond extract; blend well.;3. Stir in dates.;4. Refrigerate for 10 minutes for easier handling.;5. Form mixture into 1/2 to 1 inch balls.;6. Roll balls in powdered sugar, and place in a single layer in a large shallow container.;7. Store covered in the refrigerator.\",\"ingredients\":\"Milk Chocolate chips: oz 11.5 , is_optional: ;Vanilla wafers: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Powdered sugar: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Vanilla yogurt: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Almond extract: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Dates: oz 8 , is_optional: ;Powdered sugar:   , is_optional: ;Colored candies or sprinkles:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-6a923cb2-9f92-4ede-9da3-e5910c38a9b7\",\"name\":\"Chocolate Date Bread\",\"cooking_time\":70,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F.;2. In a large bowl, combine date-bread mix and cocoa until blended.;3. Stir in milk and egg until thoroughly combined.;4. Pour batter into a greased and floured 8 1/2 x 4 1/2-inch loaf pan.;5. Bake for 50 to 55 minutes or until a wooden pick inserted in the center comes out clean.;6. Cool bread for 10 minutes in the pan on a wire rack.;7. Remove from pan and cool completely on rack.;8. To make glaze, melt chocolate and butter, stirring constantly over very low heat until smooth.;9. Remove from heat.;10. Stir in confectioners'' sugar until stiff.;11. Stir in water until glaze is smooth and of spreading consistency.;12. Smooth glaze over bread and garnish with walnut and pecan halves.\",\"ingredients\":\"date-bread mix: oz 17 , is_optional: ;unsweetened cocoa powder: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;milk: cup 1.25 , is_optional: ;egg:  1 , is_optional: ;semisweet chocolate: oz 1 , is_optional: ;butter or margarine: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;powdered sugar: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;hot water: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Walnut and pecan halves:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-769187ab-f8d3-4925-a91a-cf614774d583\",\"name\":\"Magic Chocolate Bites\",\"cooking_time\":15,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. Melt chocolate without stirring in the top of a double boiler.;2. Remove from heat and add condensed milk, salt, and flavoring.;3. Stir only until blended.;4. Press the mixture into a block one inch high in a wax paper-lined pan.;5. Chill until firm.;6. Turn out the block of fudge from the pan.;7. Remove the wax paper.;8. Cut into serving pieces.