ut fish into 3/4-inch cubes.;4. Shell and devein shrimp.;5. Chop cabbage into bite-size chunks.;6. Clean mushrooms. If using forest mushrooms, remove and discard stems. Slice mushrooms and sprinkle with lemon juice.;7. Cut off and discard root portion of enoki mushrooms and separate clusters as much as possible.;8. Wash, trim ends, and string pea pods.;9. Clean green onions and cut in halves lengthwise, including the green portion. Cut into 2-inch lengths.;10. Clean spinach and discard thick stems.;11. To serve, arrange beef, chicken, fish, shrimp, cabbage, forest mushrooms, enoki mushrooms, snow peas, green onions, spinach leaves, water chestnuts, and bamboo shoots in individual rows on large platters or serving plates.;12. Bring broth to boil. Place a heating unit under a Chinese hot pot and pour boiling broth into the hot-pot bowl.;13. Using a Chinese wire ladle and chopsticks or fondue forks, each person places desired ingredients into the hot broth to poach.;14. When cooked (this will take only a few moments), ingredients are then dipped into sweet-and-sour sauce, soy sauce, or hot mustard as desired, and eaten with noodles, adding cilantro, if desired.\",\"ingredients\":\"boneless beef sirloin: lb 1 , is_optional: ;boned chicken breasts: lb 1 , is_optional: ;fish fillets: lb 1 , is_optional: ;medium shrimp: lb 1 , is_optional: ;Chinese cabbage: lb 1 , is_optional: ;fresh forest mushrooms: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;lemon juice:   , is_optional: ;enoki mushrooms: pk 2 , is_optional: ;Chinese pea pods: lb 0.75 , is_optional: ;green onions: bunch 2 , is_optional: ;spinach: bunch 2 , is_optional: ;canned water chestnuts: oz 8 , is_optional: ;canned bamboo shoots: oz 8 , is_optional: ;chicken broth: can 4 , is_optional: ;sweet-and-sour sauce:   , is_optional: ;soy sauce:   , is_optional: ;prepared hot Chinese mustard:   , is_optional: ;fine egg noodles: lb 0.25 , is_optional: ;cilantro or chives:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-aec3d155-b579-42dc-8e0c-6bd24e4431f6\",\"name\":\"Oriental Hot Pot\",\"cooking_time\":50,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Shortly before cooking time, arrange the prepared raw meats (shrimp, chicken breasts, beef sirloin) and vegetables (Chinese cabbage/lettuce, eggplant/water chestnuts, mushrooms) on a large tray or platter. Place the small spinach leaves in a separate bowl.;2. Set out the dunking sauces (Chinese Mustard, Ginger Soy, Peanut Sauce, Red Sauce) and provide bamboo tongs, chopsticks, or long-handled forks as cooking tools for guests.;3. Heat chicken broth in an electric skillet or chafing dish until hot. Alternatively, to use a Mongolian cooker: fill the chimney with charcoal and add charcoal starter, pour cold chicken broth into the cooker, cover, and light the charcoal.;4. Once the broth is hot and simmering (or reaches this state in the Mongolian cooker), add the chicken bouillon cubes and stir until dissolved. Then add the monosodium glutamate and grated gingerroot (or ground ginger).;5. Maintain the broth at a bare simmer for cooking, ensuring it is barely bubbling.;6. Serve with hot cooked rice. Guests will use the cooking tools to pick up desired food items, drop them into the simmering broth to cook, then lift them out and dip into the prepared sauces.\",\"ingredients\":\"Raw shrimp: lb 1 , is_optional: ;Chicken breasts:  2 , is_optional: ;Beef sirloin: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chinese cabbage: head 0.5 , is_optional: ;Eggplant: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Fresh mushrooms: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;Spinach leaves: cup 4 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: cup 5.25 , is_optional: ;Chicken bouillon cubes:  3 , is_optional: ;Monosodium glutamate (MSG): tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Grated gingerroot: tbsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chinese Mustard:   , is_optional: ;Ginger Soy:   , is_optional: ;Peanut Sauce:   , is_optional: ;Red Sauce:   , is_optional: ;Hot cooked rice:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-53306e47-a2f5-4320-b9bb-afc3cf36a635\",\"name\":\"Mongolian Hot Pot\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. Using a cleaver or sharp knife, slice the lamb into very thin slices.;2. Soak the bean thread noodles in warm water for 5 minutes, then drain them and cut them into 5-inch lengths.;3. Separate the spinach leaves from the stalks and wash them well. Discard the stalks.;4. Cut the Chinese cabbage into 3-inch pieces.;5. Combine all the ingredients for the dipping sauce (sesame paste/peanut butter, light soy sauce, rice wine/dry sherry, chili bean sauce, sugar, hot water) in a small bowl and mix them well.;6. Prepare individual settings: Each guest should have his or her own small portion of dipping sauce and a plate containing lamb, spinach and Chinese cabbage.;7. When ready to begin, bring the chicken stock to a boil and light the fondue.;8. Ladle the hot stock into the fondue pot and add the ginger, scallions, garlic, and cilantro into the stock.;9. Each person selects a piece of food (lamb, spinach, or Chinese cabbage) and cooks it quickly in the fondue pot.;10. When all the meat and vegetables have been eaten, add the prepared noodles to the pot and let them heat through.;11. Ladle the soup into soup bowls and serve.\",\"ingredients\":\"Boneless lean lamb: lb 3 , is_optional: ;Bean thread noodles: oz 4 , is_optional: ;Spinach: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chinese cabbage: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chicken stock: qt 1 , is_optional: ;ginger root: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;scallions: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;garlic: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;cilantro: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Sesame paste: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;peanut butter: tbsp 2 , is_optional: is optional;Light soy sauce: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Rice wine: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;dry sherry: tbsp 1 , is_optional: is optional;Chili bean sauce: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Sugar: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Hot water: tbsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-d92fe98e-d3a6-4f41-bf6d-f6e35d17c364\",\"name\":\"Mushroom-Potato Chowder\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Saute onions, garlic, celery, and green pepper in hot oil and margarine for about 3 minutes. Add sliced mushrooms and saute for 3 more minutes.;2. Add soymilk, dill weed, tarragon, black pepper, salt, and potatoes. Bring mixture almost to a boil; reduce heat and simmer for 25 minutes, stirring occasionally.;3. Add pureed tofu; simmer until heated through and serve.\",\"ingredients\":\"Margarine: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Vegetable oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Onion: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Mushrooms: oz 8 , is_optional: ;Garlic clove:  1 , is_optional: ;Celery: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;Green bell pepper: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;Soymilk: cup 3 , is_optional: ;Dill weed: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Tarragon: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Potatoes: cup 4 , is_optional: ;Black pepper: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Salt: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Soft tofu: oz 10.5 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-58f580bc-121f-45b6-a3ec-627b72e51712\",\"name\":\"Vegetable Noodle Stew\",\"cooking_time\":35,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Place 1/2 cup of the vegetable stock in a Dutch oven or 3 1/2 - 5 quart saucepan and bring to a boil.;2. Add onion, garlic, and ginger; simmer for 3 minutes.;3. Stir in the remaining vegetable stock and soy sauce.;4. Cover the pot and bring to a gentle boil.;5. Add bok choy, sweet red pepper, broccoli florets, carrot, sliced mushrooms, peas, buckwheat noodles, firm tofu, and watercress leaves.;6. Cook for about 8 minutes, or until noodles are softened and vegetables are crisp-tender.;7. Top each serving with one of the optional garnishes.\",\"ingredients\":\"Vegetable Stock: cup 5 , is_optional: ;Small Onion:  1 , is_optional: ;Garlic: clove 2 , is_optional: ;Gingerroot: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: tbsp 1.5 , is_optional: ;Bok Choy: stalk 3 , is_optional: ;Sweet Red Pepper:  1 , is_optional: ;Broccoli florets: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Carrot:  1 , is_optional: ;Sliced Mushrooms: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Peas: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Buckwheat Noodles: oz 2 , is_optional: ;Firm Tofu: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Watercress leaves: cup 0.25 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3e1882c7-6f6d-42d1-9fd7-26c091b5f902\",\"name\":\"Simple Tofu and Vegetables\",\"cooking_time\":30,\"servings\":3,\"instructions\":\"1. In hot oil, saute onions until limp.;2. Add bell pepper, mushrooms, tofu, sunflower seeds, water, basil, and sage to the pan.;3. Simmer until vegetables are limp.;4. Serve over cooked rice.\",\"ingredients\":\"onions:  2 , is_optional: ;bell pepper:  1 , is_optional: ;mushrooms: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;tofu: lb 1 , is_optional: ;sunflower seeds: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;water: cup 1 , is_optional: ;basil: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;sage: tsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-52af1cfb-342b-4cf3-9db6-ea31d331860c\",\"name\":\"Seasoned Vegetarian Broth\",\"cooking_time\":55,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. Rinse and thinly slice the canned Szechwan preserved vegetable.;2. Cover dried Chinese black mushrooms with hot water and let stand for 30 minutes.;3. Drain the mushrooms, cut off their stems, and reserve both stems and caps. Rinse the stems and caps.;4. In a heavy large saucepan, combine the reserved mushroom stems and caps, 4 1/4 cups cold water, the prepared Szechwan preserved vegetable, quartered green onions, coarsely chopped carrots, Oriental sesame oil, light soy sauce, black soy sauce, and ground white pepper. Bring the mixture to a boil.;5. Reduce heat, cover, and simmer for 2 hours.;6. Cool completely.;7. Refrigerate overnight.;8. Strain before using.\",\"ingredients\":\"Dried Chinese black mushrooms: piece 5 , is_optional: ;Cold water: cup 4.25 , is_optional: ;Szechwan preserved vegetable: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Green onion: piece 3 , is_optional: ;Carrots:  2 , is_optional: ;Oriental sesame oil: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Light soy sauce: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Black soy sauce: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Ground white pepper: tsp 0.125 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3fe90a7c-6ab5-45dd-960a-3797bb803ed6\",\"name\":\"Hot and Sour Garlic Chive Soup with Tofu\",\"cooking_time\":50,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. In a large heavy pot, combine carrots, fresh garlic chives, fresh lovage or celery leaves, romaine lettuce or Swiss chard leaves, dried cloud ear or shiitake mushrooms, dried arame, dulse, or tombu seaweed, fresh or dried hot red pepper, rice wine vinegar, water, dry white wine, and dark sesame oil.;2. Bring the mixture to a boil, then cover, lower the heat to medium-low, and simmer for 30 minutes.;3. Remove the mushrooms from the pot, slice them thinly, and discard any tough portions.;4. Strain the broth and return it to the pan.;5. Add the tofu and sliced mushrooms to the broth and simmer for 5 minutes.;6. Dissolve the miso in a small amount of the broth, then stir it into the soup.;7. Immediately remove the pot from the heat.;8. Garnish with minced garlic chive leaves and garlic chive flowers, and serve at once.\",\"ingredients\":\"Carrots:  2 , is_optional: ;Fresh garlic chives: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Fresh lovage or celery leaves:  3 , is_optional: ;Romaine lettuce or Swiss Chard leaves:  3 , is_optional: ;Dried cloud ear or shiitake mushrooms:  4 , is_optional: ;Dried arame, dulse, or tombu seaweed: piece 1 , is_optional: ;Fresh or dried hot red pepper:  1 , is_optional: ;Rice wine vinegar: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Water: qt 1 , is_optional: ;Dry white wine: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Dark sesame oil: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Firm tofu: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Rice or barley miso sauce: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Garlic chive leaves:   , is_optional: is optional;Garlic chive flowers:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-6f842a55-8adb-46b3-85f4-827e0d89dca0\",\"name\":\"All Veggie Soup\",\"cooking_time\":15,\"servings\":12,\"instructions\":\"1. Place all ingredients in a crockpot.;2. Cover and cook until done, about 6 hours.\",\"ingredients\":\"TVP Chunks: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Garlic cloves: clove 2 , is_optional: ;Onions: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Carrot: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Vegetable Broth Powder: tsp 5 , is_optional: ;Uncle Ben''s Converted Rice: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Hunt''s Tomatoes: can 2 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 3.5 , is_optional: ;Pinto beans: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Pepper:  0 , is_optional: ;Basil: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Green beans: can 1 , is_optional: ;Okra: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Salt:  0 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"JSWiyUKHCsDt7Ixy"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I am now deleting the \"Vegetarian Hot Pot\" recipe."},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"7Vv29mnTG7jZnepZ","name":"recipe_deleteRecipes","arguments":{"ids":["df5b6003-4eca-4433-8872-1304a910d092"]}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"recipe_deleteRecipes","content":"[{\"id\":\"df5b6003-4eca-4433-8872-1304a910d092\",\"name\":\"Vegetarian Hot Pot\",\"cooking_time\":45,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Prepare a variety of fresh vegetables such as mushrooms, tofu, leafy greens, corn, and root vegetables.;2. Prepare a flavorful vegetarian broth in a hot pot.;3. Bring the broth to a simmer and add the vegetables and tofu to cook until tender.;4. Serve hot with your favorite dipping sauces.\",\"ingredients\":\"assorted mushrooms: package 1 , is_optional: ;block firm tofu:  1 , is_optional: ;leafy greens: bunch 1 , is_optional: ;ears corn:  2 , is_optional: ;carrots:  2 , is_optional: ;vegetable broth: liter 1 , is_optional: ;soy sauce: tablespoons 2 , is_optional: ;sesame oil: tablespoon 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":1,\"allergy_tags\":null}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"7Vv29mnTG7jZnepZ"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have successfully deleted the ''Vegetarian Hot Pot'' recipe. However, this recipe is still part of a meal plan