ending on the kids'' weight.;6. Baste occasionally with a little salted water and turn spits continuously to ensure even cooking. Alternatively, use a rotisserie.;7. Add more white coals if necessary during roasting.;8. To serve, cut the roasted kid into pieces and place them on plates.;9. Garnish with guacamole, chopped white onion, finely chopped tomato, finely chopped cilantro, and finely chopped chiles serranos.;10. Serve with mashed Frijoles de Olla sprinkled with freshly grated cheese (Mozzarella or Monterey Jack), totopos, and Pico de Gallo sauce.;11. The kid may also be shredded and used in fried tacos.\",\"ingredients\":\"Kids:  2 , is_optional: ;Salt: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Mild vinegar: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Guacamole: cup 2 , is_optional: ;White onion: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Tomato: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Cilantro: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Chiles serranos: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Frijoles de Olla:  1 , is_optional: ;Cheese: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;Totopos: piece 16 , is_optional: ;Pico de Gallo sauce:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-89e9a890-c300-412f-ae31-08fe30bc3d1d\",\"name\":\"Kitty Heaven Sardines and Rice\",\"cooking_time\":5,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. Combine all ingredients.;2. Stir with a wooden spoon to break up sardines into bite-sized pieces.\",\"ingredients\":\"sardines: can 2 , is_optional: ;cooked rice: cup 0.67 , is_optional: ;liver: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;parsley: cup 0.25 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-491505e9-0ab5-425b-97be-da5b942ab470\",\"name\":\"Sweet Potato and Broccoli Medley\",\"cooking_time\":25,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. Dice the sweet potato.;2. Cook the diced sweet potato in 1/2 cup of water, covered, until almost done. Add the chopped broccoli and cook until tender. You may need to add more water during this step.;3. Add the low-fat cottage cheese and sesame seeds to the hot vegetables and toss until blended.\",\"ingredients\":\"sweet potato:  1 , is_optional: ;water: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;broccoli: cup 1 , is_optional: ;cottage cheese: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;sesame seeds: tbsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-ae1d95c1-f0f1-4501-a06f-a29b5fe19b79\",\"name\":\"Easy Crock Pot Chicken\",\"cooking_time\":480,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Place chicken in crockpot.;2. Mix together soups, and pour over chicken.;3. Cook on low, all day.;4. Serve over hot rice.\",\"ingredients\":\"chicken breasts:  4 , is_optional: ;cream of mushroom soup: can 1 , is_optional: ;cream of chicken soup: can 1 , is_optional: ;rice:  1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-5765767a-618a-4b2d-980a-67b780407001\",\"name\":\"Oatmeal\",\"cooking_time\":8,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. Mix hot water and oatmeal in a small pan.;2. Cook gently for 5-6 minutes.;3. Add raisins, cinnamon, and sunflower seeds to the cooked oatmeal.;4. Serve with low-fat milk or yogurt.\",\"ingredients\":\"Hot water: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Oatmeal: cup 0.67 , is_optional: ;Raisins: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Cinnamon: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Sunflower seeds: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Milk or yogurt: cup 0.25 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-41f6bfc5-65b2-4c19-aad2-b41e495d2a0c\",\"name\":\"Chicken Rice Burritos\",\"cooking_time\":90,\"servings\":60,\"instructions\":\"1. Combine sour cream, milk and green chilies. Chill to blend flavors.;2. Cook rice according to package directions adding cayenne pepper.;3. Stir in chicken and salt. Heat through. Cover and keep warm (150-160°F.) until ready to serve.;4. Place No. 12 scoop chicken-rice mixture on tortillas. Fold. Ladle 1/2 ounce sour cream sauce over top of folded tortillas.\",\"ingredients\":\"Sour Cream: cup 3.0 , is_optional: ;Milk: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;Green Chilies: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Uncle Ben''s Brand Chicken-Flavor Rice Pilaf: pk 1.0 , is_optional: ;Cayenne Pepper: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chicken: lb 6.0 , is_optional: ;Salt: tbsp 2.0 , is_optional: ;Flour tortillas:  60.0 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-6d1c5fc1-635d-4518-9dad-7c0694d0a2e4\",\"name\":\"Goldbeck Pocket Soup\",\"cooking_time\":10,\"servings\":18,\"instructions\":\"1. Grind split peas, cracked wheat, vegetable flakes, and seeds in a blender until they are a fine powder.;2. Combine the ground mixture with nutritional yeast and salt.;3. Store the mixture in a covered container at room temperature.;4. To use, add 1 heaping teaspoon of soup mix to 6 ounces of boiling water, or 2 level teaspoons to 1 cup of boiling water.;5. Stir, let it sit for a few minutes, and serve.\",\"ingredients\":\"split peas: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;cracked wheat: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;dehydrated vegetable flakes: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;sesame seeds: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;sunflower seeds: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;nutritional yeast: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;salt: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-19ff94b4-9c42-482d-b6a1-6349979c08ea\",\"name\":\"Tuna a La King\",\"cooking_time\":10,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. Heat soup and milk in a saucepan.;2. Add tuna and peas to the mixture.;3. Bring the mixture to a boil and then simmer for one minute.;4. Serve hot over toast points (or toast triangles).\",\"ingredients\":\"Cream of mushroom soup: can 1 , is_optional: ;Milk: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Tuna: can 1 , is_optional: ;Peas: can 1 , is_optional: ;Toast triangles:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-c5f9878b-04ba-4ac9-b20f-94264cd7d56e\",\"name\":\"Lentil Roast\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Mix all ingredients together.;2. Bake at 350 degrees Fahrenheit for 45 minutes.;3. After 45 minutes, coat the top with undiluted tomato soup and continue baking for 15 minutes more.\",\"ingredients\":\"Lentils: cup 1.33 , is_optional: ;Nuts: cup 0.67 , is_optional: ;Egg whites: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Milk: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;Applesauce: cup 0.67 , is_optional: ;Corn flakes: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Sage: tsp 0.33 , is_optional: ;Salt:   , is_optional: ;Pepper:   , is_optional: ;Onions: cup 0.67 , is_optional: ;Tomato soup:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01Dw4VowzKoDt21QX4pPiSHu"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The current recipes in your collection aren''t quite right for sick kids. Let me search for more appropriate gentle, easy-to-digest options that are traditionally recommended when children aren''t feeling well."},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"toolu_01EHvFsfbApvvEcqiVg4YRxQ","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"easy to digest meals for sick kids recipes chicken soup rice porridge toast bananas"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"For sick kids needing easy-to-digest meals, **chicken soup, rice porridge, toast, and bananas** are excellent choices due to their gentle textures and soothing properties.\\n\\n**Chicken soup** offers hydration from broth, easily digestible protein from chicken, and carbs from noodles or rice, all supporting recovery with anti-inflammatory benefits and energy. A classic chicken noodle soup with mild vegetables or a lemon chicken and rice soup variant are both comforting and nutritious.\\n\\n**Rice porridge (congee)** is traditionally recommended for its softness, ease on the stomach, and ability to incorporate mild vegetables and lean protein for extra nutrition. It is warm and bland, which soothes nausea and sore throats.\\n\\n**Toast**—preferably plain white or lightly buttered—is easy to digest as a low-fiber carbohydrate and can provide energy without upsetting sensitive stomachs. Milk toast recipes also offer gentle nourishment.\\n\\n**Bananas** are ideal as a soft fruit, packed with potassium and easy to swallow, helping maintain electrolyte balance and providing gentle nutrition.\\n\\nAdditional gentle foods for sick kids include scrambled eggs for soft protein, mashed potatoes, cooked vegetables, applesauce, and smoothies, which contribute essential nutrients in an easy-to-eat form.\\n\\n**Summary of easy-to-digest meals for sick kids based on the searched recipes:**\\n\\n| Meal Type               | Key Benefits                              | Examples/Ingredients                     |\\n|------------------------|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|\\n| **Chicken Soup**       | Hydration, protein, anti-inflammatory    | Low-sodium broth, shredded chicken, soft noodles, carrots, celery     |\\n| **Rice Porridge**      | Easy to digest, soothing, nutritious     | Soft cooked rice with mild veggies and lean protein (e.g., chicken)  |\\n| **Toast**              | Simple carbs, easy digestion              | Plain or lightly buttered white toast                              |\\n| **Bananas**            | Soft, potassium-rich, gentle on stomach  | Mashed or sliced banana                                                |\\n| **Soft Proteins**      | Protein for healing and energy            | Scrambled eggs, tofu                                               |\\n| **Other Soft Foods**   | Gentle on digestion, vitamin-rich         | Mashed potatoes, applesauce, yogurt, smoothies                     |\\n\\nThese meals help maintain hydration, nourishment, and comfort during illness with minimal digestive stress. For personalized dietary advice, consulting a healthcare professional is always recommended.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01EHvFsfbApvvEcqiVg4YRxQ"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are some wonderful easy-to-digest meals perfect for when the kids aren''t feeling well:\n\n**🍲 Classic Comfort Foods:**\n- **Chicken Soup** - The ultimate healing meal! Hydrating broth with tender chicken, soft noodles or rice, and mild vegetables. It has anti-inflammatory properties and provides gentle nourishment.\n- **Rice Porridge (Congee)** - Wonderfully soft and soothing on the stomach. You can add a little shredded chicken or keep it plain with mild seasonings.\n\n**🍞 Simple Staples:**\n- **Plain Toast** - Easy-to-digest carbs that provide energy without upsetting sensitive tummies. White bread or lightly buttered toast works best.\n- **Bananas** - Soft, naturally sweet, and packed with potassium to help maintain electrolyte balance. Can be mashed for younger kids or those with sore throats.\n\n**🥚 Gentle Proteins:**\n- **Scrambled Eggs** - Soft, mild, and easy to digest while providing important protein for recovery.\n- **Yogurt** - Smooth and cool, great for sore throats, and contains beneficial probiotics.\n\n**🥔 Other Soothing Options:**\n- **Mashed Potatoes** - Creamy and comforting\n- **Applesauce** - Gentle on the stomach and naturally sweet\n- **Smoothies** - Great way to get nutrition when they don''t feel like eating solid food\n\nAll these meals are gentle on the digestive system, help maintain hydration, and provide the nourishment kids need to recover. Would you like me to create specific recipes for any of these dishes and add them to your family collection?"}]}]',1763965766309,1763965766309,replace('- **User''s core intent**: The user wants easy-to-digest meal ideas suitable for sick children.\n- **Key actions made**: The AI searched for gentle, nourishing recipes; an initial search for suitable recipes in the user''s collection was deemed inappropriate, so the AI conducted a new search for traditional recommendations.\n- **Current state**: The AI has provided a list of easy-to-digest meal options for sick children and offered to create specific recipes for any of them and add them to the user''s collection.','\n',char(10)));
