scription":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Please refer to the recipe you just gave me and create a meal plan for the week starting tomorrow."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Oh, what a thoughtful idea! Let''s get a gentle and nourishing meal plan ready for the little ones. Here’s a proposal for the week ahead, starting tomorrow, Tuesday, November 25th, 2025. I''ve included some of those easy-to-digest meals we talked about to help them feel better.\n\n**Proposed Meal Plan (November 25th - December 1st):**\n\n**Tuesday, November 25th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Plain Toast with a Banana – A simple and energizing start.\n*   **Lunch:** Chicken Soup – Warm, hydrating, and full of goodness.\n*   **Dinner:** Rice Porridge – Soft and soothing for a gentle evening meal.\n\n**Wednesday, November 26th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Scrambled Eggs – Gentle protein to build strength.\n*   **Lunch:** Applesauce and Yogurt – Sweet, smooth, and good for a sore throat.\n*   **Dinner:** Mashed Potatoes – Comforting and easy to digest.\n\n**Thursday, November 27th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Plain Toast and a Smoothie (Banana/Yogurt) – A nourishing blend for gentle energy.\n*   **Lunch:** Chicken Soup (leftovers) – Still comforting and easy.\n*   **Dinner:** Rice Porridge – Keeping it light and easy on the tummy.\n\n**Friday, November 28th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Scrambled Eggs and Banana – Protein and potassium for a steady start.\n*   **Lunch:** Mashed Potatoes – Simple and satisfying.\n*   **Dinner:** Gentle Chicken and Rice (like boiled chicken with plain rice) – Lean protein and easy carbs for growing strength.\n\n**Saturday, November 29th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Yogurt with a side of Toast – Probiotics and simple carbs.\n*   **Lunch:** Chicken Soup – Another round of this healing classic.\n*   **Dinner:** Rice Porridge with soft, cooked vegetables (e.g., finely mashed carrots) – Adding a little more nutrition gently.\n\n**Sunday, November 30th:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Smoothie (gentle fruit blend like banana, pear) – A sweet and nutrient-rich start.\n*   **Lunch:** Scrambled Eggs and Toast – A comforting and familiar meal.\n*   **Dinner:** Mashed Potatoes with a bit of cooked, shredded chicken – A complete and easy meal.\n\n**Monday, December 1st:**\n*   **Breakfast:** Plain Toast and Applesauce – Light and easy.\n*   **Lunch:** Rice Porridge – Back to basics for continued recovery.\n*   **Dinner:** Chicken Soup – A final, comforting meal to round out the week.\n\nHow does this look? Would you like me to go ahead and create these recipes and meal plans for you, or would you like to make any adjustments?"}]}]',1763968424787,1763968424787,replace('**User''s core intent**: The user wants easy-to-digest meal ideas for sick children and a weekly meal plan based on those suggestions.\n**Key actions made**: The AI provided a list of gentle, easy-to-digest meal options after an initial search, and then created a detailed 7-day meal plan for sick kids using those items, starting tomorrow.\n**Current state**: The AI has proposed a full weekly meal plan and is awaiting the user''s feedback or confirmation to proceed with creating recipes or adjusting the plan.','\n',char(10)));
