ame":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Give me recipe of Soba with Green Beans and Beef"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"DwuUL2LLymP8IgTi","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"recipe for Soba with Green Beans and Beef"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"Here’s a simple and delicious recipe for **Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans**, inspired by several reliable sources:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### **Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans**\\n\\n#### **Ingredients**\\n- 8–12 oz (225–340g) soba noodles  \\n- 8–12 oz (225–340g) beef steak (flank, sirloin, or rump), thinly sliced  \\n- 1 lb (450g) green beans, trimmed  \\n- 1–2 tbsp vegetable or peanut oil  \\n- 1–2 cloves garlic, minced  \\n- 1 tsp fresh ginger, minced  \\n- 2–3 tbsp soy sauce  \\n- 1–2 tbsp rice vinegar  \\n- 1 tbsp mirin (optional)  \\n- 1 tsp brown sugar  \\n- 1 bunch scallions, thinly sliced  \\n- Optional: crispy shallots or sesame seeds for garnish  \\n\\n---\\n\\n#### **Instructions**\\n\\n1. **Cook the Soba Noodles:**\\n   - Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n   - Add the soba noodles and cook according to package instructions (usually 4–5 minutes).\\n   - For the last 1–2 minutes of cooking, add the green beans.\\n   - Drain and rinse the noodles and beans under cold water to stop cooking and cool them down. Set aside.\\n\\n2. **Prepare the Beef:**\\n   - Heat 1 tbsp oil in a skillet or wok over medium-high heat.\\n   - Add the beef slices and cook until browned and cooked through (about 2–3 minutes per side, depending on thickness).\\n   - Remove from pan and set aside.\\n\\n3. **Make the Dressing:**\\n   - In a small bowl, whisk together soy sauce, rice vinegar, mirin (if using), brown sugar, minced garlic, and ginger.\\n\\n4. **Assemble the Dish:**\\n   - Divide the cooled soba noodles and green beans between serving bowls.\\n   - Top with the cooked beef slices.\\n   - Drizzle the dressing over the top.\\n   - Garnish with sliced scallions and crispy shallots or sesame seeds if desired.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### **Tips**\\n- For extra flavor, you can sauté the garlic and ginger in a little oil before adding the beef.\\n- If you prefer a thicker sauce, mix 1 tsp cornstarch with 1 tbsp water and stir into the dressing before heating it slightly.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis dish is light, healthy, and full of flavor—perfect for a quick weeknight meal!\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"DwuUL2LLymP8IgTi"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Of course! Here''s a lovely recipe for **Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans** I found for you:\n\n### **Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans**\n\n#### **Ingredients**\n*   8–12 oz (225–340g) soba noodles\n*   8–12 oz (225–340g) beef steak (flank, sirloin, or rump), thinly sliced\n*   1 lb (450g) green beans, trimmed\n*   1–2 tbsp vegetable or peanut oil\n*   1–2 cloves garlic, minced\n*   1 tsp fresh ginger, minced\n*   2–3 tbsp soy sauce\n*   1–2 tbsp rice vinegar\n*   1 tbsp mirin (optional)\n*   1 tsp brown sugar\n*   1 bunch scallions, thinly sliced\n*   Optional: crispy shallots or sesame seeds for garnish\n\n#### **Instructions**\n1.  **Cook the Soba Noodles:** Cook soba noodles according to package directions, adding green beans for the last 1–2 minutes. Drain, rinse with cold water, and set aside.\n2.  **Prepare the Beef:** Heat 1 tbsp oil in a skillet or wok over medium-high heat. Cook beef slices until browned (2–3 minutes per side). Remove and set aside.\n3.  **Make the Dressing:** Whisk together soy sauce, rice vinegar, mirin (if using), brown sugar, minced garlic, and ginger in a small bowl.\n4.  **Assemble the Dish:** Divide cooled noodles and green beans into bowls. Top with beef slices, drizzle with dressing, and garnish with scallions, crispy shallots, or sesame seeds if desired.\n\nWould you like me to add this recipe to your family''s recipe collection? 😊"}]}]',1763972385337,1763972385337,replace('- **User''s core intent**: The user initially sought suggestions for 15-minute Asian-inspired dinners and then requested the recipe for a specific dish from the provided list.\n- **Key actions made**: The AI offered a list of 10 Asian-inspired dinner ideas. The user then selected "Soba with Green Beans and Beef" and the AI provided the full recipe for it.\n- **Current state**: The AI has just provided the recipe for "Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans" and is awaiting confirmation from the user to add it to their recipe collection.','\n',char(10)));
