om heat, add bonito flakes, cover and allow flakes to sink to the bottom.;4. Remove kombu and discard flakes.;5. Add tamari and mirin and lightly simmer for 1 minute.;6. Squeeze in juice from the grated ginger.;7. Place noodles in bowls and pour hot broth to cover.;8. Top with green onions.\",\"ingredients\":\"EDEN Lotus Root Soba: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 4 , is_optional: ;EDEN Kombu: strip 1 , is_optional: ;EDEN Bonito Flakes: cup 0.5 , is_optional: is optional;EDEN Organic Tamari: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;EDEN Mirin: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Grated fresh ginger: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Green onions:  2 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-61e4ab27-8737-4b3e-8dfc-07c171d65d6d\",\"name\":\"Spicy Beef Noodles\",\"cooking_time\":120,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Use a sharp knife to cut beef into 1 1/2 inch cubes.;2. Combine soy sauce, sweet bean sauce (or hoisin sauce), anise seed, cinnamon stick, orange zest, and 6 cups water in a bowl and set aside.;3. Heat a casserole or heavy pan. Add 1 teaspoon vegetable oil and heat until hot.;4. Add 3 tablespoons minced green onions, 1 1/2 tablespoons minced garlic, 1 1/2 tablespoons minced fresh ginger, and 1 teaspoon dried hot red pepper flakes to the hot pan.;5. Stir-fry until fragrant, about 10 seconds.;6. Add the soy sauce mixture and bring to a boil.;7. Add the meat cubes and return to a boil.;8. Reduce heat to low. Cover and simmer, skimming the surface to remove any impurities and fat, until the beef is tender.;9. Remove the cinnamon stick from the stew.;10. Meanwhile, bring 4 quarts (8 cups) water in a large pan to a boil.;11. Add thin egg noodles and cook until tender, about 4 minutes.;12. Drain the noodles.;13. Combine chicken broth, 1/2 teaspoon salt, and 1 1/2 teaspoons Oriental sesame oil in a large pan and bring to a boil.;14. Add fresh spinach and 3 tablespoons minced green onions (green part only) to the broth.;15. Remove from heat.;16. Portion noodles into individual serving bowls.;17. Ladle spinach and broth over the noodles.;18. Spoon beef and about 1/3 cup cooking liquid over each portion.;19. Serve Immediately.\",\"ingredients\":\"Chuck or beef stew meat: lb 2 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: cup 0.50 , is_optional: ;Sweet bean sauce: tbsp 1.50 , is_optional: ;Anise seed: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Cinnamon stick:  1 , is_optional: ;Orange zest:  1 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 14 , is_optional: ;Vegetable oil: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Green onions: tbsp 6 , is_optional: ;Garlic: tbsp 1.50 , is_optional: ;Fresh ginger: tbsp 1.50 , is_optional: ;Dried hot red pepper flakes: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Thin egg noodles: lb 0.25 , is_optional: ;Unsalted chicken broth: cup 4 , is_optional: ;Salt: tsp 0.50 , is_optional: ;Oriental sesame oil: tsp 1.50 , is_optional: ;Fresh spinach: lb 0.50 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-cb44866a-81fd-468a-856a-7b5caf206a56\",\"name\":\"Dan Dan Noodles\",\"cooking_time\":30,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Cook noodles in boiling water for about 6 minutes, then rinse and drain them.;2. Place the cooked noodles on a serving platter.;3. Lightly blanch the bean sprouts and arrange them around the noodles; set aside.;4. In a wok, heat the oil and brown the ground beef.;5. Add minced garlic, minced ginger, and horse bean sauce; stir-fry for 1 minute.;6. Add chicken broth, sherry, and soy sauce. Lower the heat to medium and cook until the liquid is reduced to half.;7. Stir in the chopped green onions.;8. In a separate small bowl, combine cornstarch and water, then stir this mixture into the hot sauce.;9. Cook until the sauce thickens.;10. Pour the thickened sauce over the noodles.;11. Garnish with Chinese parsley before serving.\",\"ingredients\":\"Beijing-style udon noodles: lb 1 , is_optional: ;bean sprouts: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Salad oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Lean ground beef: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Minced garlic: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Minced ginger root: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Horse bean sauce with chili: tsp 4.5 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;Sherry: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Light soy sauce: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Chopped green onions: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Cornstarch: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Water: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Chinese parsley:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3cd734fc-a486-4898-a35d-4fa58b7ece20\",\"name\":\"Asian Beef Noodle Soup\",\"cooking_time\":25,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Mix water, soy sauce, chili sauce, ginger, cayenne pepper, and one seasoning packet from the noodles in a large saucepan (reserve the other packet for other use).;2. Bring the mixture to a simmer.;3. Add the thinly sliced cabbage and carrots; cook for 5 minutes.;4. Add the sliced mushrooms, frozen corn kernels, and ramen noodles; simmer for 3 minutes.;5. Add the cooked round steak and thinly sliced green onions.;6. Heat through until warmed.;7. Stir in the dark sesame oil before serving.\",\"ingredients\":\"water: cup 6 , is_optional: ;soy sauce: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;chili sauce or ketchup: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;ground ginger: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;cayenne pepper: tsp 0.125 , is_optional: ;ramen instant noodle soup: pk 2 , is_optional: ;chinese or green cabbage: cup 2.5 , is_optional: ;carrots:  3 , is_optional: ;small mushrooms: cup 1 , is_optional: ;frozen corn kernels: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;round steak: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;green onions:  4 , is_optional: ;dark sesame oil: tsp 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-e78fa89c-228b-4452-8a65-889668c9ab8e\",\"name\":\"Soba Noodles with Cucumber\",\"cooking_time\":20,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Cook the noodles in a large pot of boiling water until tender. Drain well.;2. Whisk together the soy sauce, hot pepper oil, vinegar, ginger, and sesame oil and toss with the warm noodles.;3. Add the cucumber and top with the sesame seeds.;4. Serve at room temperature.\",\"ingredients\":\"soba noodles: lb 1 , is_optional: ;soy sauce: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;hot pepper oil: drop 4 , is_optional: ;white vinegar: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;fresh ginger: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;sesame oil: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;seedless cucumber:  1 , is_optional: ;black sesame seeds:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-7dde8781-bd10-4b35-b158-56209524e7ea\",\"name\":\"Dan Dan Noodles\",\"cooking_time\":35,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Cook udon noodles in boiling water for about 6 minutes, then rinse and drain them.;2. Place the cooked noodles on a serving platter.;3. Lightly blanch the bean sprouts and arrange them around the noodles; set aside.;4. In a wok, heat the salad oil and brown the lean ground beef.;5. Add minced garlic, minced ginger root, and horse bean sauce with chili to the wok and stir-fry for 1 minute.;6. Add chicken broth, sherry, and light soy sauce; lower heat to medium and cook until the liquid is reduced to half.;7. Stir in the chopped green onions.;8. In a small bowl, combine cornstarch and water, then stir this mixture into the hot sauce.;9. Cook until the sauce thickens.;10. Pour the thickened sauce over the noodles on the serving platter.;11. Garnish with Chinese parsley before serving.\",\"ingredients\":\"Beijing-style udon noodles: lb 1 , is_optional: ;bean sprouts: oz 10 , is_optional: ;Salad oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Lean ground beef: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Minced garlic: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Minced ginger root: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Horse bean sauce with chili: tsp 4.5 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;Sherry: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Light soy sauce: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Chopped green onions: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Cornstarch: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Water: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Chinese parsley:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"8VH8M0BDV8HemIQO"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That''s a super interesting question! I looked through your family''s recipes for things with soba noodles, beef, or green beans. I found a few recipes with soba noodles and a few with beef, but it looks like there isn''t a recipe in your collection that specifically combines all three of those main ingredients like ''Soba with Green Beans and Beef'' does.\n\nWould you like me to go ahead and add the ''Soba with Green Beans and Beef'' recipe to your family''s collection so you have it for future reference? 😊"}]}]',1763972810385,1763972810385,replace('-   **User''s core intent**: The user''s primary goal is to find quick Asian-inspired dinner ideas, retrieve a specific recipe ("Soba with Green Beans and Beef"), and then check if their family recipe collection contains dishes with similar ingredients.\n-   **Key actions made**: The AI provided a list of 15-minute Asian dinner options, then fetched and presented the full recipe for "Beef Soba Noodles with Green Beans." It also searched the user''s family recipe collection for recipes using soba noodles, beef, or green beans.\n-   **Current state**: The AI has provided the requested recipe and confirmed that while individual similar ingredients exist in the user''s collection, no recipe combines soba noodles, beef, and green beans. The AI is now asking if the user wants to add the new "Soba with Green Beans and Beef" recipe to their collection.','\n',char(10)));
