m_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"Chinese hot pot recipes with spicy and non-spicy broth options, and ingredients suitable for egg allergy to avoid egg allergy"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"Here are Chinese hot pot recipes with both **spicy and non-spicy broth options**, and all ingredients are **suitable for an egg allergy** (no egg or egg derivatives used).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🔥 Spicy Broth (Vegan & Egg-Free)\\n\\n**Ingredients:**\\n- 6 cups water\\n- 10–12 dried red chilies\\n- 1.5 tbsp Sichuan peppercorns\\n- 2 star anise\\n- 1 cinnamon stick\\n- 6 cloves garlic\\n- 2 tsp minced ginger\\n- 1 vegetable stock cube (egg-free)\\n- 4 tbsp hot bean paste (check label for egg-free)\\n- 1/4 cup light soy sauce (or tamari for gluten-free)\\n- 3–4 tbsp Shaoxing wine (optional, check for egg-free)\\n- Salt to taste\\n\\n**Instructions:**\\n1. Heat oil in a pot, add garlic, ginger, and spices. Fry for 1–2 minutes.\\n2. Add water, stock cube, hot bean paste, soy sauce, and wine.\\n3. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Strain if desired.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🍲 Non-Spicy (Clear) Broth (Vegan & Egg-Free)\\n\\n**Ingredients:**\\n- 6 cups water or vegetable stock (egg-free)\\n- 2–3 slices ginger\\n- 2–3 scallions, cut into large pieces\\n- 2–3 dried shiitake mushrooms\\n- 1 vegetable stock cube (egg-free)\\n- 1/4 cup light soy sauce (or tamari for gluten-free)\\n- Optional: Chinese dates (jujube), goji berries\\n\\n**Instructions:**\\n1. Add all ingredients to a pot.\\n2. Bring to a boil, then simmer for 20–30 minutes.\\n3. Strain if desired.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🥬 Egg-Free Hot Pot Ingredients\\n\\n**Vegetables:**\\n- Napa cabbage\\n- Bok choy\\n- Spinach\\n- Watercress\\n- Lotus root\\n- Carrots\\n- Corn\\n- Mushrooms (shiitake, enoki, oyster, etc.)\\n\\n**Proteins:**\\n- Tofu (silken, firm, or extra-firm)\\n- Tofu puffs\\n- Tempeh\\n- Plant-based meats (check label for egg-free)\\n\\n**Other:**\\n- Glass noodles\\n- Rice noodles\\n- Dumplings (check label for egg-free)\\n- Bean curd sticks\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🥣 Dipping Sauce (Egg-Free)\\n\\n**Ingredients:**\\n- 2 tbsp sesame paste or tahini\\n- 2 tbsp soy sauce (or tamari)\\n- 1–2 tbsp rice vinegar or black vinegar\\n- 1 tbsp vegetarian oyster sauce (check for egg-free)\\n- 1/2 tbsp sesame oil\\n- 1 tsp roasted sesame seeds\\n- 1/2–1 tbsp chili oil (optional)\\n- Chopped green onions or scallions\\n- Chopped cilantro\\n\\n**Instructions:**\\n1. Mix all ingredients in a bowl.\\n2. Adjust to taste.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 🛑 Egg Allergy Tips\\n\\n- Always check labels on packaged ingredients (soy sauce, stock cubes, plant-based meats, dumplings, etc.) for egg or egg derivatives.\\n- Avoid any sauces or products that list egg, albumin, globulin, or any egg-related ingredients.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThese recipes and ingredient lists are safe for egg allergy and offer both spicy and non-spicy broth options for a traditional Chinese hot pot experience.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"tWJ7TZIB5QQDBPyq"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That was a great idea to check for both spicy and non-spicy options! I found some fantastic Chinese hot pot recipes that will make Amy''s celebration extra special, and they are all suitable for her egg allergy. ✨\n\nHere are some ideas for your delicious hot pot:\n\n**🍲 Non-Spicy (Clear) Broth (Vegan & Egg-Free) - Perfect for Amy!**\n*   **Ingredients:** Water or vegetable stock, ginger, scallions, dried shiitake mushrooms, and a touch of soy sauce. You can also add Chinese dates or goji berries for a hint of sweetness.\n*   **How it''s made:** Simply simmer all the ingredients together for about 20-30 minutes for a flavorful, light broth.\n\n**🔥 Spicy Broth (Vegan & Egg-Free) - For a fiery kick!**\n*   **Ingredients:** Water, dried red chilies, Sichuan peppercorns, star anise, cinnamon stick, garlic, ginger, hot bean paste, and soy sauce. It''s wonderfully aromatic!\n*   **How it''s made:** Sauté the spices, then add water and other ingredients to simmer, creating a rich, spicy base.\n\n**🥚 Egg-Free Hot Pot Ingredients:**\n*   **Vegetables:** Napa cabbage, bok choy, spinach, lotus root, carrots, corn, and a variety of mushrooms like shiitake and enoki.\n*   **Proteins:** Tofu (silken, firm, or extra-firm), tofu puffs, tempeh, and plant-based meats (just double-check labels to ensure they are egg-free).\n*   **Other goodies:** Glass noodles, rice noodles, and bean curd sticks are all great additions. If you want dumplings, make sure they are egg-free.\n\n**🥣 Egg-Free Dipping Sauce:**\n*   A delicious mix of sesame paste or tahini, soy sauce, rice vinegar, a vegetarian oyster sauce (check for egg-free), sesame oil, and roasted sesame seeds. You can also add some chili oil and fresh green onions or cilantro for extra flavor.\n\nRemember to always check labels on packaged ingredients for egg or egg derivatives, especially for things like stock cubes, soy sauce, or any prepared items. I hope this helps you create an amazing celebration meal for Amy! Let me know if you''d like me to help you create a recipe with these details! 😊"}]}]',1763984256904,1763984256904,replace('**User''s core intent**: The user wants recipes for a big, spicy Chinese hot pot to celebrate Amy, who is finishing her exams.\n**Key actions made**: The AI identified that Amy doesn''t like spicy food and has an egg allergy, then successfully provided detailed, egg-free recipes for both a spicy and a non-spicy hot pot broth, along with egg-free ingredients and dipping sauce.\n**Current state**: The AI has offered a comprehensive set of recipes for a hot pot accommodating both spicy and non-spicy preferences, and Amy''s egg allergy, and is awaiting further user input.','\n',char(10)));
