,{"task_list_id":"e1671fb3-a4a9-4f8f-ac7f-60ed4dc5e180","name":"other","description":null},{"task_list_id":"1c149ac5-2027-409c-8cee-1f3f0eba294d","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"2aa82d71-b8c5-4730-a16d-53ea28207919","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"9143c0d8-5875-4e60-9eac-61cc6f730d79","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"cf27c897-d9fa-4d62-816f-ce48cc09feae","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"a67192c3-a0ce-4f70-affb-cb26d2e0cfbb","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"37aaa6cd-a28e-477d-a940-9f69122c51b1","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"ec370438-0eaf-460b-8ba9-d085f12f0b28","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"9cd41ac9-0828-418a-a16f-7cc58da185ff","name":"fdsf","description":null}]},"calendar":{"default_calendar":{"calendar_id":"f8b94cfc-9070-4814-849b-02cb0d050764","name":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Are there any shows I can watch with Amy and Noah that won''t disturb their sleep?"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"UJDd9bFUvOdASuJZ","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"calming children''s TV shows for elementary schoolers to watch before bed"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"For elementary schoolers to watch before bed, **calming children’s TV shows** are those with gentle pacing, soothing tones, soft music, and simple storylines that promote relaxation and positive social-emotional learning. Recommended shows include:\\n\\n- **Daniel Tiger''s Neighborhood** — Focuses on social-emotional skills with a calm and gentle tone.\\n- **Little Bear** — Features cozy, heartwarming stories with soft animation and calming music, ideal for bedtime.\\n- **Puffin Rock** — A nature-themed show with gentle narration and positive messages about friendship and family.\\n- **Tumble Leaf** — Whimsical, slow-paced, teaching through play with calming storylines and soothing sounds.\\n- **Kipper the Dog** — Simple plots and a slow jazzy theme song create a relaxing atmosphere perfect for winding down.\\n- **Trash Truck** — Gentle narratives emphasizing empathy and friendship with calm pacing.\\n- **Mister Rogers'' Neighborhood** — Classic calming show with predictable structure and soothing tone.\\n- **Sesame Street** — Combines education with a gentle, supportive atmosphere and calm storytelling.\\n- **Bluey** — Offers gentle humor and life lessons with calm animation, suitable for calming down before bed.\\n- **Elinor Wonders Why** and **Guess How Much I Love You** — Both praised for gentle storytelling and wholesome themes.\\n\\nThese shows avoid fast edits, loud noises, and overstimulation, making them suitable for bedtime viewing to help children relax and prepare for sleep.\\n\\nIn summary, shows like **Daniel Tiger’s Neighborhood, Little Bear, Puffin Rock, and Tumble Leaf** are particularly favored for their calming qualities and educational content that encourage positive emotions before bedtime.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"UJDd9bFUvOdASuJZ"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Of course! It''s important for Amy and Noah to get their rest, especially on a school night. Since it''s currently Tuesday, their bedtime is strictly 9:00 PM.\n\nHere are some lovely, calming shows that are great for elementary schoolers and won''t overstimulate them before bed:\n\n*   **Daniel Tiger''s Neighborhood:** This show focuses on social-emotional skills in a gentle way.\n*   **Little Bear:** Features cozy, heartwarming stories with soft animation and calming music.\n*   **Puffin Rock:** A nature-themed show with gentle narration and positive messages.\n*   **Tumble Leaf:** Whimsical and slow-paced, teaching through play with soothing sounds.\n*   **Kipper the Dog:** Simple plots and a relaxing atmosphere.\n*   **Trash Truck:** Gentle narratives emphasizing empathy and friendship.\n*   **Mister Rogers'' Neighborhood:** A classic with a predictable structure and soothing tone.\n*   **Sesame Street:** Combines education with a gentle, supportive atmosphere.\n*   **Bluey:** Offers gentle humor and life lessons with calm animation.\n*   **Elinor Wonders Why** and **Guess How Much I Love You:** Both are praised for gentle storytelling.\n\nI recommend making sure they finish watching any of these well before their 9:00 PM bedtime on weekdays to ensure they get a good night''s sleep! On Friday and Saturday nights, they have a little more flexibility, but these types of calming shows are still best for winding down."}]}]',1764053101811,1764053101811,replace('**User''s core intent**: The user initially sought evening variety shows or dramas, then shifted to asking for calming shows suitable for elementary schoolers (Amy and Noah) that won''t disturb their sleep, especially on a school night.\n**Key actions made**: The AI provided a list of evening dramas and variety/game shows for adults based on a future schedule (November 2025). Subsequently, it offered a list of calming, age-appropriate shows for children, emphasizing gentle content for pre-bedtime viewing.\n**Current state**: The AI has provided two sets of viewing recommendations: one for adults and one for elementary schoolers, with a focus on ensuring the children''s sleep is not disturbed by the content or timing of viewing.','\n',char(10)));
