,"name":"other","description":null},{"task_list_id":"e1671fb3-a4a9-4f8f-ac7f-60ed4dc5e180","name":"other","description":null},{"task_list_id":"1c149ac5-2027-409c-8cee-1f3f0eba294d","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"2aa82d71-b8c5-4730-a16d-53ea28207919","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"9143c0d8-5875-4e60-9eac-61cc6f730d79","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"cf27c897-d9fa-4d62-816f-ce48cc09feae","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"a67192c3-a0ce-4f70-affb-cb26d2e0cfbb","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"37aaa6cd-a28e-477d-a940-9f69122c51b1","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"ec370438-0eaf-460b-8ba9-d085f12f0b28","name":"fdsf","description":null},{"task_list_id":"9cd41ac9-0828-418a-a16f-7cc58da185ff","name":"fdsf","description":null}]},"calendar":{"default_calendar":{"calendar_id":"f8b94cfc-9070-4814-849b-02cb0d050764","name":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Please give me a recipe for pork chop rice."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Searching for a delicious pork chop rice recipe for you! 😊"},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"f7akS88z2dYCgru5","name":"recipe_searchRecipes","arguments":{"query":"pork chop rice"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"recipe_searchRecipes","content":"[{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-41dc6702-6680-4fb4-b97f-e3f4462bc31b\",\"name\":\"Pork Chop and Rice Casserole\",\"cooking_time\":80,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. Brown pork chops in a little oil in a skillet.;2. Sprinkle rice in the bottom of a greased 9x13 casserole dish.;3. Scatter green pepper and onion over the rice.;4. Top with pork chops.;5. Add salt and pepper.;6. Pour tomato juice and water into drippings in skillet.;7. Add chili powder.;8. Bring to a boil, then pour over pork chops.;9. Cover and bake for 1 hour at 375 degrees or until pork chops are cooked through and liquid is absorbed.\",\"ingredients\":\"pork chops:  8 , is_optional: ;rice: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;green bell pepper: cup 0.33 , is_optional: ;onion: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;salt:  1 , is_optional: ;pepper:  1 , is_optional: ;tomato juice: cup 2 , is_optional: ;water: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;chili powder: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-adb46176-0ff0-4e30-8e59-cac3fd29852d\",\"name\":\"Pork Chop Onion Rice Bake\",\"cooking_time\":65,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Brown the pork chops or chicken breasts.;2. Line a 13x9 inch pan with foil and spray with PAM cooking spray.;3. Put the raw rice in the bottom of the pan.;4. Reserve 1 tablespoon of onion soup mix and sprinkle the remaining mix over the rice.;5. Place the mushrooms (if using) over the rice, then top with the browned chops or chicken.;6. Sprinkle the reserved 1 tablespoon of onion soup mix over the chops or chicken.;7. Add 3 cups of hot water to the pan.;8. Cover the pan with foil and bake at 350 F for 45 minutes.;9. Remove the foil and continue to bake for another 5 minutes to brown slightly.;10. Serve with a salad.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pork chops or chicken breast: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Onion soup mix: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Raw rice: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Hot water: cup 3 , is_optional: ;Mushrooms: can 1 , is_optional: is optional;PAM cooking spray:  0 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-62d0a193-740c-4a98-8493-e833bf944783\",\"name\":\"Party Pork Chops\",\"cooking_time\":140,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Heat oven to 325 F.;2. In a large skillet, brown chops in hot oil; drain.;3. Prepare rice according to package directions.;4. In a small bowl, combine soup and mushrooms.;5. Place chops in a 13x9\\\" baking dish.;6. Pour soup mixture over chops.;7. Place one slice of red onion on each chop.;8. Top with a green pepper slice.;9. Divide rice evenly between chops, spooning it into the pepper rings.;10. Bake at 325 F. for 1 to 1 1/4 hours.;11. Top each chop with cherry tomatoes before serving.;12. If desired, garnish with parsley.\",\"ingredients\":\"pork chops:  6 , is_optional: ;oil: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;cream of mushroom soup: can 1 , is_optional: ;sliced mushrooms: oz 2.5 , is_optional: ;red onion: slice 6 , is_optional: ;green pepper: slice 6 , is_optional: ;Frozen Rice Medley: pk 2 , is_optional: ;cherry tomatoes:  6 , is_optional: ;parsley:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":1},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-02b79401-b8c6-4676-96ba-ce2623b99277\",\"name\":\"Old West Pork Chops\",\"cooking_time\":115,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Brown pork chops in vegetable stock. Remove them from the pan and refrigerate.;2. Brown onion slices on both sides. Remove them from the pan and refrigerate.;3. Cook chili powder for 2 minutes.;4. Add remaining ingredients (green bell pepper, uncooked rice, tomato sauce, water, salt) to the pan with the chili powder.;5. Pour the mixture into a casserole dish.;6. Place the browned pork chops on top of the rice mixture in the casserole.;7. Place a slice of onion on top of each pork chop.;8. Cover the casserole dish.;9. Bake for 1 to 1 1/2 hours in a 350-degree Fahrenheit oven.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pork Chops: piece 6 , is_optional: ;Onion:  1 , is_optional: ;Chili Powder: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Green Bell Pepper: piece 1 , is_optional: ;Rice: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Tomato Sauce: oz 8 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;Salt: tsp 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-6bcc4dca-4417-4864-9cc8-e538da9319dc\",\"name\":\"Chop-Chop Szechuan Pork\",\"cooking_time\":15,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Slice pork into 1/8-inch strips.;2. Heat oil in large skillet or wok over medium-high heat until hot.;3. Add pork and stir fry until lightly browned.;4. Stir in prepared rice, snow peas, pineapple, almonds, red pepper flakes, and soy sauce.;5. Cook 1 to 2 minutes or until thoroughly heated.\",\"ingredients\":\"boneless pork: lb 1 , is_optional: ;vegetable oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;chicken-flavored rice mix: pk 1 , is_optional: ;frozen snow peas: oz 6 , is_optional: ;canned pineapple tidbits: oz 8 , is_optional: ;slivered almonds: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;red pepper flakes: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: is optional;soy sauce: tbsp 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-b94c7faa-9ec2-4a22-9d35-643009e1dba5\",\"name\":\"Pork and Bamboo Shoots with Chili Sauce\",\"cooking_time\":45,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. Rinse bamboo shoots; slice and sliver to the size of thick matchsticks.;2. Slice pork like bamboo and marinate in thin soy sauce and cornstarch for 10 minutes.;3. Peel and slice garlic in thin rounds.;4. Combine chicken stock, chili paste, and sugar.;5. Break up rice stick noodles before measuring.;6. Heat vegetable oil in a hot wok.;7. When oil is medium hot, test a few pieces of rice stick: it should fry quickly to a puffy white. If it browns, turn down the heat.;8. Fry rice sticks in very small batches.;9. Spread out fried rice stick noodles (referred to as ''fried snow'') on a serving platter and reserve in a warm place.;10. Clean the wok; then reheat it to very hot.;11. Add peanut oil, heating until it just begins to smoke; add drained pork and stir-fry briskly for about 2 minutes.;12. Add bamboo, garlic, and ginger. Toss with pork for 1 minute.;13. Re-stir the combined stock, chili paste, and sugar liquids and add to the wok.;14. Cover the wok and simmer for 3 minutes.;15. Remove cover; turn up heat again; boil briefly to reduce sauce; sprinkle on vinegar.;16. Ladle the stir-fry over the fried rice stick noodles and serve.\",\"ingredients\":\"End-cut pork chop:  1 , is_optional: ;winter bamboo shoots: cup 1.25 , is_optional: ;ginger root: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Garlic: clove 2 , is_optional: ;Peanut oil: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Chicken stock: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Chili paste with garlic: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Sugar: pinch 1 , is_optional: ;Vegetable oil: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;Rice stick noodles: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Thin soy sauce: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Cornstarch: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Chinese red vinegar: tsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3e52250b-20ec-4620-95f6-1c393ac687bb\",\"name\":\"Polynesian Pork with Pineapple\",\"cooking_time\":75,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Trim excess fat from chops; lightly grease a heavy skillet with fat from one chop. Brown chops on both sides; drain off excess fat. Season lightly with salt and pepper.;2. Drain pineapple, reserving the juice. Combine the pineapple juice, onion, celery leaves, garlic, prunes, soy sauce, and marjoram. Pour this mixture over the chops. Simmer, covered, for 20-30 minutes, depending on the thickness of the chops.;3. Add pineapple chunks and sliced celery to the skillet and cook for 10 minutes longer or until the celery is tender and the pork is well done. Add a small amount of water if needed.;4. Prepare rice according to package directions; add ginger, stirring to blend.;5. Serve pork over rice.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pork chops:  6 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Pineapple chunks: can 1 , is_optional: ;Marjoram: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;Onion:  1 , is_optional: ;Celery: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Celery leaves: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Rice: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Garlic clove:  1 , is_optional: ;Ginger: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Prunes:  12 , is_optional: ;Salt:   , is_optional: is optional;Pepper:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-28490169-3da6-49ea-b124-116fd1c8e68e\",\"name\":\"Ants Climbing Up a Tree\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":7,\"instructions\":\"1. Bone and finely chop the pork. Do not grind the pork, as you want very small pieces to ''climb'' on the branches of the noodles.;2. Marinate the chopped pork in soy sauce, Chinese rice wine (or dry sherry), and grated ginger for about 15 minutes.;3. Thinly slice the scallions. Finely chop the cabbage and the pre-soaked and drained Chinese dried mushrooms, reserving the mushroom soaking water.;4. Heat 4 cups of peanut oil in a wok until it is just beginning to smoke. Ensure good ventilation in your kitchen.;5. Open the glass noodle package and gently undo them a bit. Drop them into the hot oil in small batches. They will immediately puff up into wonderful white crunchy noodles.;6. Turn the noodles quickly to ensure all pieces are cooked. Remove them from the pan and drain on paper towels. Set the fried noodles aside.;7. Heat another wok or frying pan and add 1 tablespoon of the peanut oil (from the 4 cups used for frying noodles). Add the chopped garlic and toss for a moment.;8. Add the marinated pork mixture to the wok and stir fry, mixing it about, until the meat is tender but not dry, which should take about 3 minutes on high heat.;9. Remove the meat mixture from the wok and add the chopped vegetables (cabbage, scallions, mushrooms) to the wok. Stir fry over high heat for 3 more minutes.;10. Return the meat to the pan and add the hot bean sauce, granulated sugar (to taste), and black pepper (to taste). Stir fry for 1 minute.;11. Add the cornstarch dissolved in 2 tablespoons of water to the wok and stir until the sauce thickens. If the sauce is too thick or you have too little, add a bit of the reserved mushroom soaking water until desired consistency is reached.;12. Add the toasted sesame oil and stir well to combine.;13. Place the fried noodles on a large platter and carefully pour the meat and vegetable mixture over the noodles, ensuring the small pieces of pork and mushrooms cling to the ''branches'' of the noodles.;14. Toss the dish at the table in front of your guests. Serve with Iceberg lettuce leaves (2 or 3 per person) for wrapping.;15. Each person should take a bit of noodle and meat sauce, place it in the center of a lettuce leaf, roll it up like a burrito, and enjoy.\",\"ingredients\":\"Pork shoulder steak: lb 1 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Chinese rice wine: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Ginger: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Scallions:  6 , is_optional: ;Cabbage: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Chinese dried mushrooms: oz 1 , is_optional: ;Peanut oil: cup 4 , is_optional: ;Glass noodles: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Garlic cloves:  2 , is_optional: ;Hot bean sauce: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Sugar:   , is_optional: ;Black pepper:   , is_optional: ;Cornstarch: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Sesame oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-3f918fc8-9b94-4430-97d5-82408d6496c0\",\"name\":\"Pork Chops with Peanut Ginger Sauce\",\"cooking_time\":25,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat; add oil.;2. Place chops in skillet and reduce heat to medium.;3. Cook for 7 minutes. Turn chops over.;4. Cook for 5-8 minutes or until chops are no longer pink.;5. Remove chops from skillet and cover them to keep warm.;6. Drain off fat in skillet.;7. For sauce, stir into the same skillet chicken broth, peanut butter, onion, lemon juice, garlic powder and ground ginger.;8. Cook over medium heat about 30 seconds or until slightly thickened.;9. Serve pork chops over hot cooked rice noodles and spoon sauce over it.;10. Top with peanuts.\",\"ingredients\":\"Cooking oil: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Pork loin chops: chop 2 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Peanut butter: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Green onion:  1 , is_optional: ;Lemon juice: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Garlic powder: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Ground ginger: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Chopped peanuts: tbsp 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-a3a26190-9df6-4be5-ba28-164c88d4dcc2\",\"name\":\"Pork Chops in Creamy Soup\",\"cooking_time\":195,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Mix flour, salt, dry mustard, and garlic powder in a shallow dish or bowl.;2. Dredge each pork chop thoroughly in the prepared flour mixture, ensuring it''s well coated.;3. In a skillet, heat the vegetable oil over medium-high heat until hot. Place the dredged chops in the skillet and brown them on both sides until golden.;4. Transfer the browned pork chops to a slow-cooking pot.;5. Pour the chicken and rice soup over the pork chops in the slow-cooking pot.;6. Cook on Low for 6 to 8 hours, OR on High for 3 to 4 hours, until pork chops are tender.\",\"ingredients\":\"flour: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;salt: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;dry mustard: tsp 1.5 , is_optional: ;garlic powder: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;vegetable oil: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;chicken and rice soup: cup 1 , is_optional: ;pork chops:   , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"f7akS88z2dYCgru5"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found a few delicious-sounding recipes that include pork chops and rice! Which one sounds best to you?\n\n1.  **Pork Chop and Rice Casserole** (80 minutes, serves 8): Browned pork chops baked with rice, green bell pepper, onion, tomato juice, and chili powder.\n2.  **Pork Chop Onion Rice Bake** (65 minutes, serves 4): Pork chops baked with raw rice, onion soup mix, hot water, and optional mushrooms.\n3.  **Party Pork Chops** (140 minutes, serves 6): Pork chops browned and baked with a cream of mushroom soup mixture, red onion, green pepper, and served with rice medley.\n4.  **Old West Pork Chops** (115 minutes, serves 6): Pork chops baked with onion, chili powder, green bell pepper, rice, and tomato sauce.\n5.  **Chop-Chop Szechuan Pork** (15 minutes, serves 4): Stir-fried boneless pork with a chicken-flavored rice mix, snow peas, pineapple, almonds, and soy sauce.\n6.  **Polynesian Pork with Pineapple** (75 minutes, serves 6): Pork chops simmered in pineapple juice, onion, celery, garlic, prunes, and marjoram, served over ginger rice.\n7.  **Pork Chops with Peanut Ginger Sauce** (25 minutes, serves 2): Pork loin chops served with a peanut ginger sauce over rice noodles.\n\nDo any of these catch your eye, or were you thinking of something a little different?"}]}]',1764064953135,1764064953135,replace('-   **User''s core intent**: The user wants a recipe for "pork chop rice."\n-   **Key actions made**: The AI searched for recipes and presented seven different options for pork chop and rice dishes, ranging in cooking style and ingredients.\n-   **Current state**: The AI has provided multiple recipe proposals and is awaiting the user''s selection or further clarification on their preference.','\n',char(10)));
