849b-02cb0d050764","name":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"My 7-year-old won''t eat anything ''green'' or ''mixed together.'' Find me 3 recipes for dinner where vegetables are hidden or seamlessly incorporated."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I understand - your little one needs recipes where the veggies are sneaky and everything stays separate! 🥕✨ Let me search for some clever dinner ideas where vegetables are hidden or kept apart so you can make mealtime easier."},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"toolu_01YahiM6YjMQsiNV3CqdJdd9","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"hidden vegetables dinner recipes for picky eaters kids vegetables not mixed"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"For picky eater kids who refuse vegetables mixed into dishes, **hidden vegetable dinner recipes that keep veggies separate or disguised** can be very effective. Some excellent ideas include:\\n\\n- **Chicken nuggets with pureed sweet potato or cauliflower blended into the nugget mixture**—the veggies are inside but not visually apparent or mixed with other veggies.\\n- **Turkey or chicken meatballs with grated or finely blended zucchini or carrots hidden inside** are flavorful and the veggies aren’t obvious on the plate.\\n- **Cauliflower or butternut squash mac and cheese**, where the veggie puree is mixed smoothly into the cheese sauce, giving flavor and nutrition without the look of vegetables.\\n- **Mini quiches or muffins with finely grated vegetables like zucchini or spinach** inside, so veggies are embedded in a familiar format.\\n- **Pizza with a cauliflower crust** or a smooth veggie-infused sauce that looks just like a regular pizza topping or sauce.\\n- **Smooth and creamy pasta sauces made from blended carrots, tomatoes, red peppers, or green veggies** where individual vegetables can''t be seen or separated.\\n- **Fruit and veggie snacks or popsicles** that mix mild-tasting veggies like carrots or beets with fruit, making them sweet and appealing to kids.\\n\\nFor picky eaters who dislike mixed vegetables visibly touching or combined, these recipes work by hiding veggies inside familiar foods or using purees in sauces rather than presenting chunks or mixed vegetable salads. This minimizes the presence of visible vegetable pieces while still delivering nutrition. Involving kids in prepping or presenting the food as a fun, favorite character or meal can also increase acceptance.\\n\\nIf vegetables truly cannot be mixed, recipes like chicken nuggets or meatballs with pureed vegetables or veggie-based sauces that appear like their favorite foods (mac and cheese, spaghetti sauce) are especially practical and popular hidden veggie options for picky kids.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01YahiM6YjMQsiNV3CqdJdd9"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Great news! I found some brilliant ideas for your little one. Here are **3 fantastic hidden-veggie dinner recipes** that should work perfectly:\n\n## 🍝 **1. Smooth Veggie Pasta Sauce with Meatballs**\nThe magic here is **blended carrot, red pepper, and tomato sauce** - it looks like a regular tomato sauce but has pureed veggies mixed in smoothly (no chunks visible!). Serve with pasta and small meatballs on the side. The sauce is creamy and delicious without any \"green\" or obvious mixed veggies.\n\n## 🍖 **2. Sweet Potato Chicken Nuggets**\nHomemade nuggets where **pureed sweet potato or cauliflower is blended into the chicken mixture** before breading. The veggie is completely hidden inside, and they look and taste like regular chicken nuggets. Serve with a favorite dipping sauce and simple sides.\n\n## 🧀 **3. Cauliflower Mac and Cheese**\nFinely **pureed cauliflower is blended into a smooth cheese sauce** - you can''t see it at all! It just makes the sauce extra creamy and nutritious. The mac and cheese tastes even better, and the veggie is completely invisible. Serve with some plain pasta on the side if needed.\n\n---\n\n**Would you like me to create detailed recipes for any of these?** I can put together full ingredient lists and step-by-step instructions so you can make them right away! Just let me know which one(s) sound best! 😊"}]}]',1764680399237,1764680399237,replace('- **User''s core intent**: The user wants 3 dinner recipes for a 7-year-old who won''t eat green or mixed vegetables, where vegetables are hidden or seamlessly incorporated.\n- **Key actions made**: The AI searched for and provided 3 suitable recipes: Smooth Veggie Pasta Sauce, Sweet Potato Chicken Nuggets, and Cauliflower Mac and Cheese.\n- **Current state**: The AI has presented three recipe options with brief descriptions and is awaiting the user''s selection to provide detailed recipes.','\n',char(10)));
