ription":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Snack"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"toolu_01BXEktyXxzHg3USmkS2goDc","name":"recipe_searchRecipes","arguments":{"query":"fruit yogurt"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"recipe_searchRecipes","content":"[{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-b6b98c45-29d2-4a72-8098-e9e5665565f5\",\"name\":\"Frozen Fruit Yogurt Pops\",\"cooking_time\":285,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. Puree yogurt and fruit in a blender. Once the fruit is well blended, add honey and blend again.;2. Pour the mixture into a freezer-safe container, such as an ice cube tray, a shallow plastic container, or a 9-inch square cake pan.;3. Freeze for 30 minutes.;4. Spoon the partially frozen mush back into the blender container and whip for 1 minute until smooth.;5. Pour the whipped mixture into popsicle molds or paper cups.;6. Freeze for 10 more minutes and then return to the freezer until firm.\",\"ingredients\":\"homemade yogurt: cup 2 , is_optional: ;frozen or fresh fruit: cup 1 , is_optional: ;honey: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;vanilla: tsp 1.50 , is_optional: ;cinnamon: tsp 0.50 , is_optional: ;nutmeg: tsp 0.50 , is_optional: ;frozen juice concentrate: oz 6 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-9f9b1efe-d5d2-440f-b80c-067bfcd8057d\",\"name\":\"Yogurt Fruit Salad\",\"cooking_time\":65,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Combine the sliced banana and diced apple in a bowl.;2. Cut the orange over the bowl to catch any juice, then add the orange chunks to the bowl.;3. Stir the fruit mixture well (the orange juice will help delay browning of the apple and banana).;4. Stir in the well-drained crushed pineapple, sliced green grapes, and yogurt.;5. Chill the fruit salad for at least 1 hour before serving.\",\"ingredients\":\"Banana:  1 , is_optional: ;Red apple:  1 , is_optional: ;Eating orange:  1 , is_optional: ;Canned unsweetened crushed pineapple: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Seedless green grapes: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Low-fat vanilla yogurt or low-fat plain yogurt: cup 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-4669ca98-145a-45d9-95e3-475bc41fed03\",\"name\":\"Frozen Apricot Yogurt\",\"cooking_time\":150,\"servings\":8,\"instructions\":\"1. In a small saucepan or microwave dish, combine dried apricots with orange juice.;2. Bring to a boil. Cover and simmer over medium heat for 10 to 12 minutes OR cover and microwave at High power for 7 minutes, or until apricots are softened.;3. Puree the apricot mixture in a food processor or blender, or pass through a food mill.;4. Let the puree cool completely.;5. Combine the cooled apricot mixture, low-fat yogurt, and grated orange rind. Mix well.;6. Freeze the mixture in an ice-cream machine or transfer to a shallow metal cake pan. Freeze until almost solid.;7. Break the almost solid mixture into big chunks and beat with an electric mixer or food processor until smooth.;8. Transfer the mixture to an airtight container and freeze until firm (about 30 minutes to 1 hour).;9. Before serving, let stand in the refrigerator for 15 to 30 minutes or until softened.\",\"ingredients\":\"dried apricots: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;orange juice: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;low-fat yogurt: cup 3 , is_optional: ;grated orange rind: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;fresh fruit or berries:  0 , is_optional: is optional;fresh mint leaf:  0 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-88dafaef-1ec1-4d9a-939e-d7bce26b13d6\",\"name\":\"Strawberry Yogurt Freeze\",\"cooking_time\":385,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Stir the yogurt if it is not premixed.;2. Spoon the yogurt into ice cube tray compartments.;3. Freeze until completely frozen, 3 or 4 hours.;4. Remove the frozen yogurt cubes from the tray, place them in the bowl of an electric food processor, and process until finely chopped.;5. Add the stemmed strawberries and grated orange peel to the food processor.;6. Process just until the mixture is almost smooth.;7. Serve immediately or place in the freezer and stir occasionally until firm enough to scoop, 1 to 2 hours.\",\"ingredients\":\"low-fat strawberry yogurt: oz 8 , is_optional: ;strawberries: pt 1 , is_optional: ;grated orange peel: tsp 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ac657fd1-93ad-4a81-9ef0-b518bd6d4d23\",\"name\":\"Berries with Sweet Yogurt\",\"cooking_time\":5,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. In a blender, combine the low-fat plain yogurt, sugar, low sugar jam, and orange or lemon zest.;2. Blend until smooth.;3. Serve the sauce over the sliced strawberries or other berries.\",\"ingredients\":\"yogurt: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;sugar: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;low sugar jam: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;strawberries: cup 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":3},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-dcb8b0d7-8343-4d88-aef5-06665c888c7f\",\"name\":\"Greek Yogurt\",\"cooking_time\":0,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"\",\"ingredients\":\"Greek Yogurt:  1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-d9495306-af32-48ee-a0a7-c2286dea9f22\",\"name\":\"Berries with Sweet Yogurt\",\"cooking_time\":5,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. In a blender, combine the low-fat plain yogurt, sugar (if using), low sugar jam, and orange or lemon zest.;2. Blend until smooth.;3. Serve the sauce over the sliced strawberries or other berries.\",\"ingredients\":\"Yogurt: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Sugar: tsp 1 , is_optional: is optional;Low sugar jam: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Orange zest: dash 1 , is_optional: ;Strawberries: cup 2 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-43cdba6c-57eb-4c5b-a92f-14ca8e1eec7c\",\"name\":\"Fruity Yogurt Freeze\",\"cooking_time\":5,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. In a food processor or blender, combine all ingredients; cover and blend on high speed about 1 minute or until smooth.;2. Pour into tall glasses.\",\"ingredients\":\"Nonfat vanilla yogurt: oz 8 , is_optional: ;Canned unsweetened pineapple: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Canned sliced peaches: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Ice cubes: unit 5 , is_optional: ;Banana: unit 1 , is_optional: ;Skim milk: cup 0.25 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"b1d2f993-f2a1-497e-8f46-8589d66c3fe4\",\"name\":\"Yogurt\",\"cooking_time\":0,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. Serve 1 cup plain yogurt;2. Can be topped with fruit or granola\",\"ingredients\":\"yogurt: cup 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"2d81cbea-5639-4adc-920b-acbfadd82656\",\"name\":\"Yogurt with Applesauce\",\"cooking_time\":0,\"servings\":2,\"instructions\":\"1. Spoon plain yogurt into a bowl or cup.;2. Top with unsweetened applesauce.;3. Stir together gently if desired, or keep in layers.;4. Serve immediately as a cool, soothing treat.\",\"ingredients\":\"plain yogurt: cup 1 , is_optional: ;unsweetened applesauce: cup 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":2}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01BXEktyXxzHg3USmkS2goDc"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I found a lovely simple \"Yogurt Fruit Salad\" recipe that would be great for snacks! 🍓 Here''s what I''m proposing:\n\n**Your Snack Plan:**\n- **Dates:** Wednesday (Dec 3), Thursday (Dec 4), and Friday (Dec 5)\n- **Meal Type:** Snack ✨\n- **Dish:** Yogurt Fruit Salad\n- **Why it''s perfect:** It''s colorful, sweet, refreshing, and packed with real fruit! No added sugars, just the natural sweetness of bananas, apples, oranges, grapes, and pineapple mixed with creamy yogurt. Your teeth will love it! 🦷💕\n\nDoes this sound good to you? Should I go ahead and add it to your meal plan for all three days?"}]}]',1764733893761,1764733893761,replace('-   **User''s core intent**: The user initially wanted the AI to secretly add candy to their dinner. After the AI offered alternatives, the user''s intent shifted to planning a mom-approved, tooth-friendly fruit yogurt snack for three days.\n-   **Key actions made**: The AI declined to add a secret dessert and proposed tooth-friendly options. The user chose fruit yogurt and specified it as a snack. The AI then formulated a specific "Yogurt Fruit Salad" plan.\n-   **Current state**: The AI has presented a detailed "Yogurt Fruit Salad" snack plan for three days (Wednesday-Friday) and is awaiting the user''s final confirmation to add it to their meal plan.','\n',char(10)));
