me":"Family Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"15-minute Asian-inspired dinners"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I''d love to help you find some quick Asian-inspired dinner ideas! 🍜 Let me search for some delicious 15-minute options for you."},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"toolu_01MxXEZ9iAmmrhpMBUU2KzhU","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"15-minute Asian-inspired dinner recipes quick easy"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"Here are several **quick and easy Asian-inspired dinner recipes that can be made in 15 minutes or less**:\\n\\n- **Korean Tuna Mayo Rice Bowl (Deopbap)**: Made with rice, canned tuna, garlic butter, vegetables, and drizzled with mayo and sweet soy sauce. Perfect for a fast, flavorful meal.\\n\\n- **Chinese Ground Beef Rice Bowl**: Uses ground beef with bold, savory Asian flavors served over rice, ready in 15 minutes.\\n\\n- **Udon Noodle Soup**: Quick soup with udon noodles, leftover turkey (or chicken), bok choy, and miso broth for a cozy dinner.\\n\\n- **Thai Stir-Fried Noodles (Pad See Ew)**: A classic Thai dish made with wide rice noodles, Chinese broccoli, and a savory soy-based sauce, ready faster than takeout.\\n\\n- **Thai Chili Basil Chicken Stir Fry**: Quick stir-fry with chicken, chili, garlic, and basil for spicy, fresh flavor; regular basil can substitute Thai basil.\\n\\n- **Mapo Tofu (Japanese style)**: A quick Sichuan-inspired spicy tofu dish with less oil, providing a flavorful vegetarian option.\\n\\n- **15-Minute Korean Noodle Soup**: A hearty, flavorful one-pot noodle soup with simple ingredients and pantry leftovers.\\n\\n- **15-Minute Creamy Korean Chicken Ramen**: A rich ramen soup with chicken and Korean flavors, quick to prepare.\\n\\n- **Sweet & Spicy Hoisin Cashew Chicken**: Ready in about 30 minutes but simple enough for a fast meal with hoisin sauce, cashews, and chicken.\\n\\n- **Garlic Butter Prawns with Soy Sauce**: A fast stir-fry combining garlic butter and soy, ideal for prawns.\\n\\n- **Thai Coconut Chicken Soup (Tom Kha Gai)**: Bright, fresh, and easy with tender chicken and coconut milk, usually around 15-30 minutes.\\n\\n- **Spam Ramen (10-Minute)**: Turns pantry staples into quick and satisfying ramen with Spam and noodles.\\n\\nMost of these recipes emphasize fresh vegetables, simple proteins (chicken, tofu, beef, prawns), and quick cooking techniques like stir-frying, soups, and noodle dishes that can be made from scratch in under 15 minutes using everyday ingredients.\\n\\nIf you want truly fast Asian-inspired dinners, focus on rice or noodles as a base, quick-cooking proteins, fresh or frozen vegetables, and flavor enhancers like soy sauce, hoisin, oyster sauce, chili, garlic, and sesame oil. Woks or large skillets facilitate speedy cooking.\\n\\nVideos and downloadable recipes are available for many of these dishes from sources like Marion’s Kitchen and YouTube channels focused on 15-minute Asian meals for step-by-step guidance.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01MxXEZ9iAmmrhpMBUU2KzhU"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Here are some fantastic **15-minute Asian-inspired dinners** you can whip up:\n\n✨ **Quick & Easy Options:**\n\n1. **Thai Stir-Fried Noodles (Pad See Ew)** - Wide rice noodles with Chinese broccoli and savory soy sauce. Faster than takeout! 🍜\n\n2. **Thai Chili Basil Chicken Stir Fry** - Spicy, fresh, and packed with flavor. Amazing with just chicken, chili, garlic, and basil\n\n3. **Korean Tuna Mayo Rice Bowl** - Canned tuna with garlic butter, veggies, mayo, and sweet soy sauce over rice. Super simple! 🍚\n\n4. **Chinese Ground Beef Rice Bowl** - Bold, savory flavors served over rice in just 15 minutes\n\n5. **Udon Noodle Soup** - Cozy and quick with noodles, bok choy, and miso broth. Great for leftover proteins\n\n6. **Thai Coconut Chicken Soup (Tom Kha Gai)** - Bright, creamy, and aromatic. Ready in 15-30 minutes\n\n7. **Garlic Butter Prawns with Soy** - Fast stir-fry that''s elegant and delicious\n\n8. **Mapo Tofu** - Spicy, flavorful vegetarian option that''s ready in minutes\n\n**💡 Pro Tips:**\n- Use a wok or large skillet for fast cooking\n- Keep pantry staples on hand: soy sauce, hoisin, oyster sauce, chili, garlic, and sesame oil\n- Rice or noodles as your base makes it super quick\n- Fresh or frozen vegetables work perfectly\n\nWould you like me to create any specific recipe from this list for your family, or search for more details on a particular dish? 😊"}]}]',1764734186409,1764734186409,replace('-   **User''s core intent**: The user requested 15-minute Asian-inspired dinner ideas.\n-   **Key actions made**: The AI confirmed the request, used a tool to find options, and then provided a list of 8 specific 15-minute Asian-inspired dinner suggestions with brief descriptions and pro tips.\n-   **Current state**: The AI has presented a list of quick dinner options and is now awaiting the user''s choice to either generate a specific recipe or provide more details on a particular dish.','\n',char(10)));
