nghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not our family. We''re having guests over this weekend, but they''re from China and don''t really like anything too sweet."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"toolu_01AAPLgZ4tyFn9aZe3UxCMF6","name":"system_intelligentSearch","arguments":{"query":"healthy snacks for picky eaters not too sweet savory options"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"system_intelligentSearch","content":"{\"search_summary\":\"Healthy savory snacks are excellent for picky eaters who want to avoid overly sweet options. Here are some great choices that combine nutrition with appealing flavors:\\n\\n## Vegetable-Based Options\\n\\n**Roasted vegetables** offer a satisfying crunch without added sugar. Crispy roasted chickpeas are particularly popular—you can enjoy them simply with olive oil and salt, or dress them up with shawarma spices or everything bagel seasoning for a fun twist. Similarly, roasted pumpkin seeds provide a crave-worthy crunchy snack when tossed with olive oil and salt, and you can add chili powder or smoked paprika for extra flavor.\\n\\nFor those who enjoy leafy greens, **cheesy kale chips** baked with nutritional yeast offer a healthier alternative to potato chips with half the calories. Air fryer sweet potato chips and air fryer butternut squash fries with hot honey are also quick and satisfying options.\\n\\n## Protein-Rich Choices\\n\\n**Eggs** make an excellent protein-packed snack. Basil and olive eggs—hard-boiled eggs stuffed with basil and Kalamata olives—provide a boost of protein and work as either a snack or light lunch. Cottage cheese-based options like baked cottage cheese eggs are also protein-rich alternatives.\\n\\nFor cheese lovers, **Parmesan crisps** made with just one ingredient are low in carbs, ready in minutes, and deliver crispy, cheesy flavor.\\n\\n## Dips and Spreads\\n\\n**Hummus** is a versatile daily snack that pairs perfectly with carrot sticks or rice cakes. You can also try **spicy aubergine dip with carrot dippers**—a low-calorie, low-fat option that counts toward your daily vegetable intake. Other dip options include caramelized onion dip, chili cheese dip, and homemade falafel.\\n\\n## Simple Savory Snacks\\n\\n**Popcorn** offers a quick, customizable option that''s healthy, vegan, and gluten-free when seasoned with rosemary, garlic, and chili. It''s also ready in just 10 minutes and endlessly customizable. **Stovetop popcorn** tossed with butter, sea salt, and nutritional yeast provides addictive savory, cheesy flavor.\\n\\nOther straightforward options include lightly salted mixed nuts, string cheese, and sea salt beef jerky for those who eat meat.\"}","success":true,"tool_call_id":"toolu_01AAPLgZ4tyFn9aZe3UxCMF6"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Here are some healthy, savory snacks that Chinese guests (and picky eaters in general) will love—no overly sweet stuff! 😊\n\n**Vegetable-Based Snacks:**\n- **Roasted chickpeas** - crispy and satisfying with just olive oil, salt, and maybe some chili powder or everything bagel seasoning\n- **Roasted pumpkin seeds** - great with salt, chili powder, or smoked paprika\n- **Kale chips** - baked with nutritional yeast for a cheesy, crispy vibe\n- **Air fryer sweet potato or butternut squash fries** - naturally savory\n\n**Protein-Packed Options:**\n- **Hard-boiled eggs** - classic, filling, and easy to prepare ahead\n- **Parmesan crisps** - literally just cheese, baked until crispy (ready in minutes!)\n- **Hummus** with carrot sticks or rice crackers - pairs perfectly with veggies\n\n**Other Favorites:**\n- **Stovetop popcorn** - toss with butter, sea salt, and nutritional yeast for savory, cheesy flavor\n- **Mixed nuts** - lightly salted (almonds, cashews, etc.)\n- **Beef jerky** - if your guests eat meat\n- **Spicy eggplant dip** with carrot dippers - low-cal and delicious\n\nThese are all easy to prepare ahead, look impressive on a snack board, and are genuinely tasty without being overly sweet. Would you like me to create recipes for any of these, or help you plan a snack spread for Saturday or Sunday? 🎉"}]}]',1764906361545,1764906361545,replace('**User''s core intent**: The user wants healthy snack ideas for upcoming guests from China who do not like overly sweet food.\n**Key actions made**: The AI clarified the target audience for snack suggestions, and then provided a list of savory, healthy snack options suitable for Chinese guests who prefer less sweetness.\n**Current state**: The AI has provided a list of specific snack suggestions and is now offering to create recipes for any of them or help plan a snack spread for a specific day (Saturday or Sunday).','\n',char(10)));
