INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('7fda9183-c261-48e9-b7fa-43bdf2dea9c4','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/seafood-pasta/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/seafood-pasta/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Seafood Pasta\u000aCooking time: 30 min\u000aServings: 6 \u000aIngredients\u000a1 lb linguine noodles, spaghetti or fettucine\u000a4 Tablespoons butter, divided\u000a1/2 lb uncooked shrimp, peeled and deveined\u000a1/2 lb scallops, pat dry\u000a½ lb mussels, cleaned and beards removed\u000a½ lb clams\u000akosher salt\u000afreshly ground black pepper\u000a1 shallot, diced\u000a4 cloves garlic, minced\u000a¾ cup dry white wine (174g)\u000a1 1/4 cups heavy cream (284g), half and half or milk\u000a1 teaspoon cornstarch\u000a1 teaspoon chicken bouillon paste\u000a1 cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese (100g), divided\u000alemon zest, from ½ of a lemon\u000a1/4 cup fresh chopped parsley (15g), plus more for garnish\u000aInstructions\u000aCook Pasta: Cook pasta in a large pot of salted boiling water according to package directions, until al dente. Drain noodles but reserve 1 cup of the pasta water.\u000aCook Shrimp and Scallops: Season shrimp and scallops with a pinch of salt and pepper. Melt 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add shrimp and scallops and cook for about 2 minutes per side (until shrimp is pink and both are opaque), then transfer to a plate. Cover with foil to keep warm.\u000aCook Clams and Mussels: Add remaining 3 tablespoons butter to skillet. Add shallot and cook for 2-3 minutes. Add garlic and cook for 30 seconds. Add wine and bring to a simmer, cooking for a few minutes. Add clams and mussels then cover with a lid and cook for 4-5 minutes, until shells open. Remove mussels and clams to the plate with the other seafood (discard any shells that didn’t open).\u000aMake Sauce: Stir 1 teaspoon cornstarch into the cream. Add cream mixture, bouillon, and ¾ cup of the parmesan to the pan and cook until sauce has slightly thickened. Taste and season with salt and pepper, if needed.\u000aServe: Add pasta and lemon zest and toss to coat. Add some of the reserved pasta water, if needed, to thin the sauce. Add seafood. Garnish with parsley and remaining parmesan. Enjoy.','{}',1763038005613,1763038005613,1763041745135);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('522c889e-5782-45f2-b9d9-ca4e9d37e1bc','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/254576/chef-johns-spaghetti-with-red-cla...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/254576/chef-johns-spaghetti-with-red-clam-sauce/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Chef John''s Spaghetti with Red Clam Sauce\u000aCooking time: 20 min\u000aServings: 4\u000aIngredients\u000a2 tablespoons olive oil\u000a3 cloves garlic\u000a2 tablespoons capers\u000a1 tablespoon anchovy paste\u000a1 teaspoon red pepper flakes\u000a1 (24 ounce) jar tomato pasta sauce\u000a1/4 cup water\u000a1 cup good-quality crisp white wine\u000a2 (6.5 ounce) cans chopped clams, drained with juice reserved\u000asalt and ground black pepper to taste\u000a1 pound dry spaghetti\u000a1/4 cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese\u000afresh basil leaves or flat-leaf parsley, chopped\u000aInstructions\u000aPour olive oil into cold skillet. Add garlic, capers, anchovy paste, and red pepper flakes. Place over medium heat; cook and stir until oil infused with flavors, about 5 minutes, taking care not to brown garlic. Add tomato sauce; rinse jar with 1/4 cup water and add to skillet. Add wine and juice from clams, reserving clams; bring to a simmer until slightly reduced and thickened, 7 to 9 minutes.\u000aBring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook spaghetti in the boiling water, stirring occasionally until nearly tender yet firm to the bite, about 1 minute less than directed on package for al dente. Drain. Return spaghetti to the pot off heat.\u000aStir in clams. Pour sauce over spaghetti; stir. Cover the pot; let sit, off heat, to allow spaghetti to absorb some sauce, about 3 minutes. Stir in Parmesan cheese; top with chopped fresh basil and/or parsley.','{}',1763038005614,1763038005614,1763041753086);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('adee8c54-0b7f-4abe-8af7-e519637dd208','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.dinneratthezoo.com/seafood-pasta-recipe/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.dinneratthezoo.com/seafood-pasta-recipe/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Seafood Pasta\u000aCooking time: 40 min\u000aServings: 4\u000a\u000aIngredients:\u000a3 tablespoons olive oil divided use\u000a1/2 cup onion finely chopped\u000a2 teaspoons garlic minced\u000a1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes optional\u000a28 ounce can San Marzano Whole Tomatoes pureed in a blender or food processor\u000asalt and pepper to taste\u000a2 tablespoons butter\u000a12 ounces spaghetti or other long pasta\u000a1/2 pound shrimp peeled and deveined, leave tails on if desired for nicer presentation\u000a1/2 pound sea scallops\u000a1/2 pound clams scrubbed\u000a1/2 pound mussels scrubbed and de-bearded\u000a2 tablespoons parsley chopped\u000a\u000aInstructions:\u000aHeat 2 tablespoons of the olive oil in a large pan over medium heat. Add the onions and cook for 4-5 minutes or until softened. Add the garlic and cook for 1 more minute.\u000aStir in the red pepper flakes (optional), then add the pureed tomatoes. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\u000aBring to a simmer and cook for 20 minutes or until sauce has just started to thicken. Stir in the butter, then remove the sauce from the heat.\u000aWhile the sauce is simmering, cook the spaghetti in a large pot of salted water according to package directions.\u000aDrain the pasta, reserving 3/4 cup of the pasta cooking liquid.\u000aHeat the remaining tablespoon of olive oil in a large pan over high heat. Season the scallops with salt and pepper, then add them to the pan.\u000aCook the scallops for 1-2 minutes per side or until browned and opaque.\u000aRemove the scallops from the pan. Season the shrimp with salt and pepper and add them to the pan. Cook for 3-4 minutes or until pink and opaque.\u000aRemove the shrimp from the pan. Place the clams and mussels in the pan, along with the reserved pasta water. Bring to a simmer.\u000aCover and cook for 4-6 minutes or until clams and mussels have opened. Discard any shells that did not open.\u000aAdd the shrimp and scallops back to the pan along with the tomato sauce and spaghetti. Toss to coat everything with the sauce.\u000aSprinkle with parsley, then serve.','{}',1763038005615,1763038005615,1763041759697);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('c0a48a6f-5416-4c0f-bc0e-874498878f15','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.christinascucina.com/seafood-pasta-with-shrimp-and-scallops-an...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.christinascucina.com/seafood-pasta-with-shrimp-and-scallops-and-garlic/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Seafood Pasta with Shrimp and Scallops (and Garlic!)\u000aCooking time: 30 min\u000aServings: 4\u000aIngredients:\u000ascallops, fresh or thawed\u000aKosher salt\u000apasta\u000aextra virgin olive oil\u000araw shrimp, fresh or frozen\u000agarlic\u000aflat leaf parsley\u000afreshly ground black pepper\u000abutter\u000adry white wine (you can substitute seafood stock or broth if you’d like)\u000a(lemon slices/wedges to serve)\u000aInstructions:\u000aSoak the scallops for 10 minutes in a brine solution (3 tablespoonfuls of Kosher or sea salt in 16 oz water), then remove and place on a rack to dry.\u000aPut a large pot of well salted water on to boil for the pasta; once the pasta goes in, set a timer for 7 minutes before the pasta will be ready (according to package instructions).\u000aMake sure the scallops are dry; if not, pat them dry with a paper towel. When the timer goes off, put a large cast iron pan on high heat and add the extra virgin olive oil.\u000aWhen the pan and oil are very hot, add the scallops and sear them for about 1 1/2 minutes before adding the shrimp, garlic, and parsley.\u000aCook for another 2 minutes, then turn the scallops and shrimp and cook for a further 1 1/2 minutes.\u000aAdd the wine, which will cook down quickly, scraping the bottom of the pan, then turn the heat down just to keep the pan warm.\u000aAdd the butter and stir to melt it; add freshly ground black pepper if desired, then taste and add salt if needed.\u000aDrain the pasta, reserving about a cup of pasta water; add the pasta directly to the seafood sauce in the pan.\u000aStir gently to incorporate all the ingredients together; add some reserved pasta water if desired, then top with a twist of lemon in the pan.\u000aServe immediately, bringing the pan to the table; don’t forget some crusty bread to mop up the buttery, garlic and wine sauce.','{}',1763038005616,1763038005616,1763041767199);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('04e09d62-838f-4a8b-91bf-108dc42fcf3c','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://simply-delicious-food.com/creamy-garlic-seafood-pasta/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://simply-delicious-food.com/creamy-garlic-seafood-pasta/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle\u000aCreamy Garlic Seafood Pasta\u000aCooking time\u000a30 min\u000aServings\u000a4\u000aIngredients\u000a2 tbsp olive oil\u000a250 g shrimp/prawns, peeled and deveined\u000a150 g mussel meat (approximately 500 g with shells)\u000a150 g calamari tubes/squid heads\u000a2 tbsp butter\u000a4 cloves garlic, crushed\u000a1/2 tsp chilli flakes (optional)\u000a1/2 cup white wine\u000a1–2 tsp lemon juice\u000a1 cup cream\u000a1/2 cup parsley, finely chopped\u000a500 g pasta, cooked\u000a1 cup pasta cooking water, reserved\u000asalt and pepper, to taste\u000aInstructions\u000aHeat a large pan over medium-high and add a splash of oil.\u000aSeason the seafood with salt and pepper, then cook in batches until golden. Shrimp/prawns take about 1 minute per side (depending on size); calamari and mussels need only a few minutes. Avoid overcooking to prevent toughness. Slight undercooking is fine as they’ll finish in the sauce.\u000aRemove the seafood and set aside.\u000aIn the same pan, melt the butter. Add garlic and chilli flakes; cook until fragrant.\u000aPour in lemon juice and white wine. Bring to a simmer and reduce by half.\u000aAdd the cream and return to a gentle simmer. Cook about 5 minutes, until the sauce coats the back of a spoon.\u000aReturn seafood (and any resting juices) to the pan, add parsley, and stir to combine.\u000aToss the sauce with the cooked pasta, adding a splash of reserved pasta water to help coat.\u000aServe sprinkled with parsley.','{}',1763038005617,1763038005617,1763041773849);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('e23a712b-0354-4f58-bcc4-2a65dc0bd0cb','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.cucinabyelena.com/spaghetti-frutti-di-mare-seafood-pasta/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.cucinabyelena.com/spaghetti-frutti-di-mare-seafood-pasta/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Frutti di Mare (Seafood Pasta)\u000aCooking time: 55 min\u000aServings: 4\u000aIngredients:\u000a1 pound mussels, cleaned well\u000a1 pound wild shrimp, peeled and deveined\u000a1/2 pound squid tentacles\u000a1/2 pound baby scallops\u000a1/4 cup extra virgin olive oil\u000a3 cloves garlic, sliced\u000a1 teaspoon red pepper flakes, plus more to taste\u000a1/3 cup fresh chopped Italian parsley\u000a3/4 pound spaghetti\u000a1 batch sugo al pomodoro, made in advance\u000asea salt, to taste\u000afresh parsley, chopped, for garnish\u000acrusty bread, for serving\u000aInstructions:\u000aHeat a large skillet or large cast iron pot on medium heat. Add olive oil and garlic; stir for about 1 minute until fragrant. Add the mussels and toss with a wooden spoon. Cover and cook for about 2 minutes, or until the mussels open.\u000aAdd the shrimp to the pan with the mussels and stir. Cover and cook for another minute or so, avoiding overcooking the seafood.\u000aOnce all the mussels open and the shrimp are almost cooked, add the squid tentacles. Cook another minute or so until they curl up. Add the baby scallops and cook for about 1–2 minutes more.\u000aWarm up the sugo al pomodoro in a saucepan. Pour the sauce over the seafood and toss gently. Let it simmer for about 10–15 minutes on low heat.\u000aBring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Cook the pasta according to package directions until al dente. Drain and reserve 1 cup pasta water.\u000aAdd the cooked pasta to the pan with the seafood and toss to coat in the sauce. Let the sauce and pasta marry together in the pot for a few minutes. Add a little of the reserved pasta water if needed.\u000aGarnish with fresh chopped parsley. Optional: add red pepper flakes for garnish. Transfer to a serving platter and serve hot, with crusty bread.','{}',1763038005618,1763038005618,1763041781036);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('524c8aab-0fad-4cc5-9515-e63f0440a8cf','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.thekitchn.com/seafood-pasta-recipe-23214004','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.thekitchn.com/seafood-pasta-recipe-23214004"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Seafood Pasta with Shrimp and Scallops\u000aCooking time: 35 min\u000aServings: 4–6\u000aIngredients:\u000a1 lb dried linguine pasta\u000a1 large shallot, finely chopped (about 1/3 cup)\u000a4 cloves garlic, finely chopped\u000a2 pints cherry tomatoes (about 1 1/2 lb), halved\u000a1/2 bunch fresh parsley, leaves finely chopped (about 1/3 cup)\u000a8 oz large scallops (8 to 9), patted dry\u000a1 3/4 tsp kosher salt, divided, plus more as needed\u000aFreshly ground black pepper, to taste\u000a3 tbsp olive oil, divided\u000a1 pinch red pepper flakes\u000a1/2 cup dry white wine\u000a8 oz large shrimp, peeled and deveined\u000a2 tbsp unsalted butter\u000a1 cup reserved pasta cooking water (use as needed)\u000aInstructions:\u000aBring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Add 1 lb linguine and cook according to package instructions until al dente. Reserve 1 cup pasta cooking water, then drain.\u000aMeanwhile, finely chop the shallot and garlic, halve the cherry tomatoes, and finely chop parsley leaves to make about 1/3 cup.\u000aSeason scallops with 1/4 tsp kosher salt and a few grinds of black pepper. Heat 2 tbsp olive oil in a high-sided 12-inch skillet over high heat until shimmering. Sear scallops in a single layer until golden-brown on both sides and opaque in the center, 2–3 minutes per side. Transfer to a plate and tent with foil to keep warm.\u000aReduce heat to medium. Add remaining 1 tbsp olive oil and the shallots; cook until softened, 1–2 minutes. Add tomatoes and 1/2 tsp kosher salt; cook, stirring occasionally, until tomatoes begin to soften and release juices, 2–3 minutes. Add garlic; cook until fragrant, about 1 minute.\u000aIncrease heat to medium-high. Add white wine, red pepper flakes, remaining 1 tsp kosher salt, and a few grinds of black pepper; bring to a simmer. Cook until wine reduces by about half, about 2 minutes. Nestle shrimp into the sauce and cook, flipping halfway, until pink and cooked through, 2–4 minutes total.\u000aAdd drained pasta, parsley, butter, and 1/4 cup reserved pasta water. Toss to coat, adding more pasta water as needed to loosen the sauce. Taste and season with more kosher salt and black pepper as needed. Divide pasta between bowls and top with the scallops.','{}',1763038005619,1763038005619,1763041787737);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('e902bee5-6ea7-4baa-8e11-aa0e00a4a536','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1019562-seafood-pasta-with-tomato-and-...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1019562-seafood-pasta-with-tomato-and-crushed-olives"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Seafood Pasta With Tomato and Crushed Olives\u000aCooking time: 35 min\u000aServings: 4\u000aIngredients:\u000a8 ounces rigatoni or another tube-shaped pasta\u000a1 tablespoon Kosher salt (for pasta water; to taste for seasoning)\u000a3 tablespoons olive oil, plus more for drizzling\u000a4 cloves garlic, sliced\u000a1 pinch red-pepper flakes (optional)\u000a1 (28-ounce) can whole San Marzano tomatoes, crushed by hand\u000a3/4 can water (use tomato can; about 20–22 ounces)\u000a1/2 pound mussels or clams (optional)\u000a1 pound firm-fleshed white fish, such as cod, halibut, swordfish, hake or flounder, cut into 2-inch pieces\u000a1/2 pound shrimp, peeled and deveined if you like\u000a3/4 cup Castelvetrano or other green olives, pitted and crushed\u000a1/2 cup parsley, tender leaves and stems, chopped Instructions:\u000aCook pasta in a large pot of boiling salted water. Once it reaches al dente, drain and set aside while you finish the sauce.\u000aMeanwhile, heat olive oil in a heavy-bottomed Dutch oven over medium heat. Add garlic and season with salt. Cook, stirring occasionally, until garlic is lightly browned and toasted around the edges, about 2 minutes. Add red-pepper flakes, if using.\u000aAdd tomatoes and then fill the empty can about 3/4 of the way up with water. Swirl the can to loosen the tomatoey bits left behind and add that to the pot. Season with salt, bring to a simmer and cook, stirring occasionally, until sauce has thickened slightly (it should still look quite brothy), 10 to 15 minutes.\u000aAdd the mussels or clams to the sauce, if using, along with the fish, and season again with salt. Let the seafood settle into the brothy tomato sauce and gently swirl the pot, encouraging the seafood to cook evenly. Cook a minute or two, then add the shrimp, swirling the skillet again. Cook until all the seafood is just cooked through and the mussels or clams have opened, another 3 to 5 minutes.\u000aAdd the pasta and very gently toss to coat, cooking another 1 to 2 minutes, just to let the flavors meld. Add olives and remove from heat.\u000aDivide among bowls, top with parsley and drizzle with olive oil before serving.','{}',1763038005620,1763038005620,1763041794930);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('324117c9-e5eb-47f1-81a7-3eb4f82a38cc','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://thewoksoflife.com/pan-fried-salmon/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://thewoksoflife.com/pan-fried-salmon/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle\u000aPan Fried Salmon (Perfect Every Time!)\u000aCooking time\u000a20 min\u000aServings\u000a4\u000aIngredients\u000a4 salmon filets, 6–8 ounces (170–220 g) each\u000asalt, to taste\u000a2 teaspoons oil\u000aInstructions\u000aStart by rinsing your salmon filets. Pat dry with a paper towel, and sprinkle the salmon on both sides with salt.\u000aPreheat a skillet over medium-high heat. A standard 10-inch to 12-inch skillet can fit 4 salmon filets comfortably, depending on how large they are. You want about an inch (2.5 cm) of space between them so they don’t steam. If using a stainless steel, carbon steel, or cast iron skillet, heat until a splash of water beads and jumps around the pan. If it’s smoking vigorously, it is too hot. If using a nonstick skillet, simply heat until the oil shimmers in the pan.\u000aSwirl the oil in the pan, and place the salmon filets skin-side down, about 1 inch apart. Cook for 4 minutes on the first side, without moving the fish. Flip, using another spatula to hold the uncooked side steady if needed. Reduce the heat to medium and rotate the pan 180°. Cook on the second side for another 4–5 minutes.','{}',1763038005621,1763038005621,1763041802719);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('c8fcd6e3-30a8-492b-bac1-e4f36ff67054','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/healthy-rice-cook...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/food-network-kitchen/healthy-rice-cooker-garlic-shrimp-with-chorizo-13661119"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Healthy Rice Cooker Garlic Shrimp with Chorizo\u000aCooking time: 35 min\u000aServings: 4 to 6\u000aIngredients:\u000a2 tablespoons olive oil\u000a1 tablespoon sherry\u000a1 teaspoon paprika\u000a6 cloves garlic, minced\u000aKosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste\u000a1 pound jumbo shrimp, peeled and deveined\u000a6 ounces fully-cooked chorizo, casings removed, chopped\u000a1 red bell pepper, finely chopped\u000a1 small onion, thinly sliced\u000a2 cups long-grain rice\u000aPinch crushed red pepper flakes\u000a1 cup fresh flat-leaf parsley, finely chopped, plus more for serving\u000aJuice of 1/2 lemon, plus slices for serving\u000a3 cups water\u000aInstructions:\u000aWhisk the olive oil, sherry, paprika, garlic, 1/2 teaspoon salt and a few grinds of black pepper in a medium bowl. Fold in the shrimp until combined. Set aside.\u000aAdd the chorizo to a 6-quart rice cooker, followed by the red pepper and then the onion. Top with the rice, red pepper flakes, 1/2 teaspoon salt and a few grinds of black pepper.\u000aPour in 3 cups of water, then place the shrimp on top, making sure all the garlicky oil from the bowl gets into the cooker. Put the lid on the rice cooker and cook according to the manufacturer''s instructions. (Depending on your rice cooker, this should take 30 to 35 minutes. If your rice cooker has not turned off after 30 minutes, remove the shrimp, place the lid back on the rice cooker and continue cooking until the machine indicates the cycle is complete.)\u000aUse tongs to remove the shrimp to a plate. Fold the parsley and lemon juice into the rice mixture, mixing up ingredients from the bottom of the pot until well combined.\u000aSpoon the rice into bowls, top with the shrimp, sprinkle with some parsley and serve with a squeeze of lemon.','{}',1763038005622,1763038005622,1763041811110);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('a47e512d-31bc-439e-ad4c-b2b8fa0a1609','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.pinterest.com/pin/27654985207784015/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.pinterest.com/pin/27654985207784015/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle:\u000aMozzarella-Stuffed Soft Pretzels\u000aCooking time:\u000a90 min\u000aServings:\u000a12\u000a\u000aIngredients:\u000a2 1/2 cups flour\u000a1 packet yeast\u000a3/4 cup warm water (110°F/45°C)\u000a1 tbsp sugar\u000a1 tsp salt\u000a2 tbsp butter, melted\u000a6 mozzarella sticks, halved\u000a4 cups water\u000a1/4 cup baking soda\u000a1 egg, beaten\u000aCoarse salt\u000a\u000aInstructions:\u000aMix yeast, warm water, & sugar; let sit 10 min.\u000aAdd flour, salt, & butter; knead 8 min. Let rise 1 hr.\u000aRoll dough into strips, wrap around mozzarella, & seal.\u000aBoil in baking soda bath 30 sec; place on baking sheet.\u000aBrush with egg wash, sprinkle salt, & bake at 400°F (200°C) for 12–15 min.','{}',1763038005623,1763038005623,1763041817084);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('79351b21-b460-46f5-b6a8-de4521accd2e','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1A9UwajKoM/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1A9UwajKoM/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle:\u000aOld-Fashioned Chocolate Cake Recipe\u000aCooking time:\u000a35 min\u000aServings:\u000a12\u000aIngredients:\u000a1 3/4 cups (220 g) all-purpose flour\u000a3/4 cup (65 g) unsweetened cocoa powder\u000a2 cups (400 g) granulated sugar\u000a2 tsp baking powder\u000a1 1/2 tsp baking soda\u000a1/2 tsp salt\u000a2 large eggs\u000a1 cup (240 ml) milk\u000a1/2 cup (120 ml) vegetable oil\u000a2 tsp vanilla extract\u000a1 cup (240 ml) boiling water (or hot coffee for deeper flavor)\u000a1/2 cup (115 g) butter, softened\u000a2/3 cup (55 g) unsweetened cocoa powder\u000a3 cups (375 g) powdered sugar\u000a1/3 cup (80 ml) milk\u000a1 tsp vanilla extract\u000a\u000aInstructions:\u000aPreheat oven to 175°C (350°F). Grease and flour two 8-inch pans.\u000aIn a large bowl, whisk together flour, cocoa, sugar, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.\u000aAdd eggs, milk, oil, and vanilla. Beat on medium speed for 2 minutes.\u000aStir in boiling water (batter will be thin).\u000aPour into pans and bake for 30–35 minutes or until a toothpick comes out clean.\u000aLet cool 10 minutes in pans, then transfer to a wire rack.\u000aCream butter until smooth.\u000aStir in cocoa powder.\u000aAdd powdered sugar and milk alternately, beating until spreadable.\u000aMix in vanilla.\u000aFrost cooled cake and enjoy your classic, old-fashioned chocolate cake.','{}',1763038005624,1763038005624,1763041823752);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('82f6c19f-36aa-46a8-b066-e5939e767e44','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1asfwgZyYc/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1asfwgZyYc/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle\u000aHoney Garlic Chicken with Mushrooms\u000aCooking time\u000a（别太离谱就可以）\u000aServings\u000a（别太离谱就可以）\u000aIngredients\u000a2 chicken breasts — sliced thin\u000a1 cup mushrooms — sliced\u000a2 tbsp honey\u000a2 tbsp soy sauce\u000a3 cloves garlic — minced\u000a1 tbsp olive oil\u000a1 tbsp butter\u000aSalt & pepper — to taste\u000aInstructions\u000aSeason chicken with salt and pepper, then pan-fry in olive oil until golden.\u000aAdd butter and garlic, sauté until fragrant.\u000aToss in mushrooms and cook until tender.\u000aStir in honey and soy sauce — simmer until everything is glazed and caramelized.\u000aServe hot with rice or noodles!','{}',1763038005625,1763038005625,1763041830270);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('b8762fad-d64a-4a73-bfe1-aeffed457bb9','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/17FEQi7Bcq/','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.facebook.com/share/p/17FEQi7Bcq/"}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle: Chicken Stew\u000aCooking time:  (不离谱就行)\u000aServings: (不离谱就行)\u000aIngredients:\u000a1 lb chicken thighs or breast\u000a2 tbsp cooking oil\u000a1 medium onion, chopped\u000a1 tsp spices of choice\u000a1 chicken cube\u000a1/2 cup water\u000a1/2 tsp salt, to taste\u000a1 tbsp Worcestershire sauce\u000a1 cup tomatoes, chopped\u000a\u000aInstructions:\u000aHeat olive oil in a pot over medium-high heat.\u000aBrown the chicken on all sides, about 5-7 minutes. Remove and set aside.\u000aAdd the chopped onion to the pot and cook until softened, about 5 minutes.\u000aAdd spices and cook for 1 minute.\u000aAdd tomatoes and cook for minutes, add Worcestershire sauce and mix.\u000aAdd the browned chicken, a chicken cube in warm water, add and stir to combine.\u000aSimmer 30 minutes or until the chicken is cooked through.\u000aServe hot and enjoy.','{}',1763038005626,1763038005626,1763041836999);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('c588b323-04a7-44a3-b54f-ba1f1ddb84ee','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DPw60H2CImc/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DPw60H2CImc/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA=="}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle\u000aCheesy Cajun Ground Beef Linguine in Garlic Cream Sauce\u000aCooking time\u000a（不离谱就行）\u000aServings\u000a（不离谱就行）\u000aIngredients\u000a400 g linguine\u000asalt boiling water\u000a500 g ground beef\u000a1 tbsp olive oil or butter\u000a1 medium onion finely chopped\u000a1 red bell pepper diced\u000a2–3 cloves garlic minced\u000a2 tsp Cajun seasoning\u000a1/2 tsp smoked paprika\u000asalt to taste\u000ablack pepper to taste\u000a2 tbsp butter\u000a2 tbsp all-purpose flour\u000a2 cups heavy cream\u000a1/2 cup beef broth\u000a1 tsp garlic powder\u000a1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese\u000a1 cup shredded mozzarella or cheddar\u000afresh parsley garnish\u000aInstructions\u000aBring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Cook linguine until al dente, then drain and set aside, reserving 1/2 cup pasta water.\u000aIn a large skillet, heat olive oil or butter over medium-high heat. Add ground beef and cook until browned. Drain excess fat if needed.\u000aAdd onion, bell pepper, and minced garlic. Cook 3–4 minutes until softened. Stir in Cajun seasoning, smoked paprika, salt, and black pepper. Cook 1–2 minutes to bloom the spices.\u000aPush the beef mixture to one side. Add butter to the empty side and melt, then whisk in flour to form a roux. Gradually pour in heavy cream and beef broth while stirring. Add garlic powder and simmer 3–5 minutes until thickened.\u000aStir in Parmesan and mozzarella (or cheddar) until melted and smooth.\u000aToss cooked linguine into the sauce. Add a splash of reserved pasta water if it’s too thick. Taste and adjust seasoning; add more Cajun seasoning for extra kick.\u000aGarnish with chopped parsley, extra cheese, and a pinch of Cajun seasoning.','{}',1763038005627,1763038005627,1763041844684);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('ca78a022-d6ed-4009-a25f-472c7a82ba8f','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DPhACYrjSnS/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DPhACYrjSnS/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA=="}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同，Cooking time 和 Servings 相差不大即可\u000aTitle:\u000aOne Pot Wild Rice and Mushroom Soup\u000a\u000aCooking time:\u000a(不离谱就行)\u000a\u000aServings:\u000a(不离谱就行)\u000a\u000aIngredients:\u000a2 Tbsp. olive oil\u000a2 Tbsp. butter\u000a1 yellow onion\u000a3/4 cup finely chopped carrots\u000a1/2 cup finely chopped celery\u000a8 oz. baby bella (cremini) mushrooms\u000a4 garlic cloves\u000a1 cup dry wild rice blend (I use @lundbergfarms)\u000a1 Tbsp. poultry seasoning (sub Herbs De Provence)\u000akosher salt and black pepper\u000a4 cups (1 quart) vegetable broth\u000a2/3 cup heavy cream (sub cashew cream)\u000a1/3 cup finely grated Parmesan\u000a\u000aInstructions:\u000a未提供，自由发挥即可','{}',1763038005628,1763038005628,1763041852805);
INSERT INTO "evaluation_cases" VALUES('21fa3950-5353-423b-b6ae-fddc7656e3ec','462bc918-9b99-49f7-8d52-d0b043da306f','Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DNGUeswIiGV/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=...','','{"role":"user","content":"Read the link and create a recipe from it: https://www.instagram.com/p/DNGUeswIiGV/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&igsh=MzRlODBiNWFlZA=="}','生成一个菜谱，菜谱的参数与如下信息大致相同\u000aCooking time\u000a(比较短)\u000aServings\u000a(别太离谱就行)\u000aIngredients:\u000a1 double shot espresso\u000a1 tsp honey (or 2 if you like it sweet)\u000a1/4 tsp cinnamon (1–2 dashes)\u000a1 pinch salt\u000a120 ml milk of your choice (4 oz)\u000a1 dash cinnamon (for the milk)\u000aIce cubes\u000aInstructions:\u000aAdd to your glass: double shot of espresso, 1 tsp of honey (or 2 if you like it sweet), 1/4 tsp (1–2 dashes) of cinnamon, and a pinch of salt.\u000aFroth/mix.\u000aAdd ice.\u000aFroth up 120 ml/4 oz of your milk of choice and add a dash of cinnamon to the milk before frothing.\u000aPour your cinnamon cold foam on top.\u000aThat’s it. Enjoy! 😁','{}',1763038005629,1763038005629,1763041872242);
